MID_END_Solo_XDead_Cmn_001: Died in battle at {Variable=3},\non {Variable=1}/{Variable=2}, in the year {Variable=0}.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Kai_001: Hoping to make the world a better place,\nCai entered the service of Divine Sovereign\nJurah, who was planning the restoration of\nthe Dagdan Empire. Already known as a\nhero, Cai swiftly climbed the ranks and\nbecame a general in the Dagdan army.\nHe was idolized by his troops but always\nkept {AvatarName}'s advice at heart.\nThe records say that a person in white who\nsometimes visited him was always received\nas warmly as one of Cai's own family.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Bel_001: Bertrand moved quickly to realize his dream\nof a Dagdan Alliance. He first secured the\nsupport of Arago. Once control of western\nDagda was consolidated under him, he\nbegan his campaign to replace the empire\nas ruler of the land. As king of the Dagdan\nAlliance, Bertrand patiently negotiated with\nthose who resisted his ideas. He always\nkept the "strength in being human" that\n{AvatarName} referred to in mind,\nthough he never again encountered the\nPromised One during his reign.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Dit_001: Dietrich set off with {AvatarName} on\ntheir journey to aid people. While drifting\nthrough the land of Dagda, they occasionally\nclashed as violently as if they intended to\nkill each other. The white-clad Promised\nOne and black-clad swordsman drew\nattention wherever they went, piquing the\npeople's curiosity, but the pair's otherworldly\nair kept people at a distance. All who saw\nthem agreed that it was impossible to tell\nwhether they hated each other with all their\nhearts or trusted each other implicitly.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Tal_001: Talimun returned to his busy life as the\nchief executive of the Vandahl Trading\nCompany, and the company entered a\ngolden age. Even after saying his farewell to\n{AvatarName}, he made full use of the\ncompany's resources to support the\nPromised One in secret. {CapitalizeNextLetter}{AvatarName}\noccasionally visited Talimun, and when this\nhappened, Talimun dropped everything to\ngive his full attention. The two of them had\npassionate discussions on the future of the\nworld, lasting all through the night.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Orh_001: {CapitalizeNextLetter}{AvatarName} and Orchel traveled the\nland together. Wherever they went, Orchel\nsowed flower seeds, praying humbly that\nthey might bring some small comfort to\nhearts weighed down by Balor. Those who\nsaw the pair said they cared for each other\ndeeply, like lifelong lovers. But one day,\nOrchel vanished from {AvatarName}'s\nside, and another woman was seen in her\nplace. These two settled on a hill\noverlooking the sea, where they spent\nmany years together.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Seo_001: Even after the great war for humanity,\nTheodora worked tirelessly for Saramis.\nUnder her rule, the people came together to\nrestore the kingdom, quickly rising to their\nprevious heights. She also achieved her\npeople's long-held dream when the temples\napproved the annexation of Cybele.\n{CapitalizeNextLetter}{AvatarName} was always by Theodora's\nside, quietly watching over her from the\nshadows. Only her beloved got to see her\nsofter side at the end of each day when her\nqueenly duties were complete.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Led_001: Even after the war with Balor, chaos was\nrampant throughout Dagda, and the people\nstill suffered. {CapitalizeNextLetter}{AvatarName} set out on a\njourney to bring light to them. Feigning\ninnocence, Leda set out the same way, with\na different method—she soothed wounded\nhearts with her music, as she once said she\nwould. Though she insisted it was mere\ncoincidence, the two traveled their odd path\ntogether for a long time. {CapitalizeNextLetter}{AvatarName}\nseemed to understand Leda well and met\nher rationalizations with a gentle nod.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Anh_001: After two hundred years of hardship,\nAnatolia completed Tiamat. Just before\nascending into space, Anatolia was reunited\nwith {AvatarName}, who confirmed their\nlove remained undiminished. Yet Anatolia\nhonored the will of her beloved, who chose\nto stay on earth, and decided to part ways.\n"Whenever you look at the sky, remember\nme," she said. "I will always be there."\nAnatolia and the Promised One shared a\npassionate embrace before parting. Her\npeople came to be known as the celestials.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Tia_001: Tialla took {AvatarName} to Ribeira\nto introduce them to her grandpa. Even the\nGreat August was impressed with their\nknowledge, and the two discussed many\nthings over the next several days. For her\npart, Tialla grew jealous and threw herself\neven deeper into her studies to broaden\nher knowledge. She later proved herself a\nremarkable tactician, but even at her\nbusiest, she made time for the sporadic\nvisits from {AvatarName}.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Pet_001: Keeping their promise, {AvatarName}\nremained always at Peter's side. But the\npostwar world was still a chaotic one, and\ndisturbing rumors abounded. Remembering\n{AvatarName}'s inspiring nature, Peter\nsuggested the two of them set out on a\nmission to help people. When asked if he\nwas sure, Peter nodded firmly and insisted\non accompanying {AvatarName}, saying\n"I can't accept being the only one who's\nhappy. Besides, no matter what happens,\nI'll always have you."
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Hur_001: After defeating Balor, {AvatarName}\ncontinued traveling ceaselessly to aid the\npeople suffering from the continued chaos\nin the world. Ultand, who left Aurora's side,\nstuck close to them in support of their goal.\nThe times when she would make too much\nfood in her trusty pot were, for her, the\nhappiest moments of her life. Whenever she\nhad the chance to visit family, the mood\nwas raucous as her younger siblings\ndemanded stories of the Promised One.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Max_001: Due to injuries sustained while protecting \n{AvatarName} in their travels, Maxim\nwas unable to fight again. Feeling like a\nburden, Maxim left {AvatarName}'s side,\nbut his clothing became very popular and\nhis business took off. After a few years,\nMaxim was a successful tailor. When a\ntraveler in white visited his shop, Maxim\nsmiled proudly and showed off all the outfits\nhe'd prepared for the occasion. "My job is\nto provide you with clothes," he grinned,\n"no matter how often you ruin them."
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Gol_001: Goliath remained in Dagsion, still spending\nhis days as a gladiator entertaining crowds.\nHe was no longer the man feared as the\nButcher, letting his rage get the better of\nhim. His new fighting style, focused on\nputting on a show for spectators, became\nthe trend in the arena, and Goliath rose to\nfame as its most popular practitioner.\n{CapitalizeNextLetter}{AvatarName} would always stop by\nwhenever their mission of salvation took \nthem to Dagsion, and Goliath was happy to\nsee them every time.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Gat_001: Gaitz set off far to the east, in high spirits\nwith {AvatarName} at his side. After a\njourney spanning several years, the two\nreached the land of Sai. They tracked down\ndetails on an elixir of immortality and made\nfor an island across the sea, but decades of\nsearching proved fruitless. Gaitz, feeling the\neffects of old age, begged {AvatarName}\nto return and help the king as his final\nrequest. With a grateful smile on his lips,\nGaitz closed his eyes for the last time.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Dan_001: Even after the final battle, chaos continued\nto reign. {CapitalizeNextLetter}{AvatarName} set out to quell\nthe people's suffering, and Dante went with\nthem in the name of "research." She was\nso utterly dedicated that she kept records of\n{AvatarName}'s every move. Twenty\nyears later, feeling her strength waning,\nDante returned alone to Dagsion to write a\nplay about the Promised One, entitled The\nEnvoy of the Sun. She spent 30 years\ncompleting it, making it her magnum opus.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Fab_001: {CapitalizeNextLetter}{AvatarName} invited Fabio to join them\non their journey to offer the people aid. In\nthese long years, Fabio quickly became\nknown as the Promised One's chief disciple,\nand this didn't seem to displease him. When\nthe body Fabio had borrowed reached its\nlimit, he began to talk of parting, feeling\nsure that the Promised One would object to\nhim taking a new body. With a rueful smile,\nhe admitted that if they found themselves in\nconflict down the road, the Promised One\nmight not even realize it was him.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Esm_001: Esmeralda returned to her hometown with\n{AvatarName} to make their living as\nfishers. However, they increasingly became\nknown for driving off attacks from bandits\nand sea beasts, leaving Esmeralda, who\nlonged for a humbler life, dissatisfied.\nAfter 10 years, Esmeralda sent the\nPromised One out, saying, "Go on. There are\nstill lots of folks out there who need you."\nHer face said more—that she wanted\nthem to visit sometimes. {CapitalizeNextLetter}{AvatarName}\nsmiled kindly at her in understanding.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Urs_001: Ursula continued to work hard as manager\nof the Vandahl Trading Company. After 50\nyears, she eventually left the company.\nWatching the land of Dagda recede from the\ndeck of a Fódlan-bound ship, she laughed at\nherself for returning to a homeland she had\nno intention of seeing again. "This must\nstrike you as funny. Regardless, I wanted to\nwalk with you one last time, in the land of\nmy birth." As she lowered her eyes, a figure\nin white stood next to her, smiling gently.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Sim_001: Simon decided to go with {AvatarName}\non their journey, doing battle wherever they\nwent over many years. History records\nSimon as the first disciple to fight alongside\nthe Promised One. In one battle, however,\nhe took a blow meant for {AvatarName},\nwhich proved fatal. "This is pretty much\nhow I thought I'd go," he said. "At least it\nwas never boring with you." These were\nSimon's final words as {AvatarName}\nlooked on. He was said to have worn a\nsatisfied expression as he passed.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Lou_001: {CapitalizeNextLetter}{AvatarName} resolved to stay in\nDagsion for a time, watching over Ludia.\nAfter seeing some of her hopes fulfilled,\nthey confessed they were going on a journey\nof salvation. Ludia agreed to accompany\nthem, and the two set out. Many Vandahl\nTrading employees were sad to see her go,\nbut as was typical for her, she stood firm in\nthe face of their pleas. Wherever they went,\nLudia recorded accounts of their feats in\nbooks, which became important resources\nfor future scholars of the Promised One.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Fia_001: Fianna chose to go with {AvatarName}\non their journey of salvation. She took great\npains to care for the injured wherever she\nfound them, eventually coming to be known\nas a saint. She revered {AvatarName}\nwith all her heart, and {AvatarName}\nunderstood her more deeply than anyone.\n"All doors are open to me with you at my\nside," she confessed to them once. "So keep\nme close...or else."
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Die_001: After many years at Credna's temple, Diego\nset out to unite his kin, who had become\naimless wanderers. Years passed, and true\nto his promise to {AvatarName}, Diego\nrose to prominence as a strong chieftain. In\ntime, he led not only the Har Hali but other\nforest peoples as well. It wasn't long before\nthe Har Hali under Diego had grown into\na force far greater than before. From time to\ntime, {AvatarName} would visit, and\nwas warmly welcomed on these occasions.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Lor_001: As they promised Loretta, {AvatarName}\nchose to stay by her side until her dream\ncame true. Despite nearly giving up several\ntimes, with {AvatarName}'s help, Loretta\neventually built an orphanage in Dagsion\nthat sheltered many children. Yet Loretta\nstill felt dissatisfied, sensing that her\nbeloved would soon leave now that her\ndream had been realized. Promising to\nreturn, {AvatarName} set off on a\njourney of salvation, to aid people all over\nDagda in need of help.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Set_001: {CapitalizeNextLetter}{AvatarName} accepted Seteth's\nproposal and crossed the sea to Fódlan.\nSeteth offered his services as a guide, but\n{AvatarName} knew many things even\nhe did not, leaving Seteth sometimes struck\nwith awe. Before long, Seteth realized he\nhad a deep respect for {AvatarName}.\nEventually they parted, and it is believed\ntheir paths never crossed again. Amidst his\nduties at Garreg Mach, Seteth sometimes\nfound himself thinking of the lone savior\nin white.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Nin_001: As Ninae accompanied {AvatarName}\non their journey, she gradually became more\nin tune with her emotions. Strangely, she\nsometimes mistook {AvatarName} for a\nparent. They traveled the land to quell the\nchaos, slaying Demonic Beasts and bandit\ngangs when necessary, but also bringing\noppressive local lords to justice. In time,\nword spread of the Promised One and their\nblack-clad follower. The spirits watched\nover the pair with a certain pride, as if\nbestowing blessings upon them.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Bon_001: Bonaventure returned to Saramis and busied\nhimself using his skills to the fullest to\nrebuild the country and nurture the next\ngeneration. All the while, he dreamed of\nreuniting with {AvatarName} within his\nlifetime, never forgetting the promise the\ntwo of them had exchanged. Ten years later\nwhen he was ill, he was visited by a figure\nin white. Bonaventure was deeply moved\nand passed away while under their care.\nThose who knew him said that his dying\nexpression was one of great joy.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Tob_001: The lively feast that Tobias threw to\ncelebrate {AvatarName}'s return was\nattended by many and lasted three days and\nthree nights. They celebrated\n{AvatarName}'s deeds and the end of the\nchaos that had engulfed the world. After\nthat, Tobias returned to Saramis and lived a\nfull life as a commander—one sometimes\nvisited by a figure in white. Unusually for\nTobias, he never again forgot\n{AvatarName}'s name.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Lil_001: {CapitalizeNextLetter}{AvatarName} accompanied Lilian to\nher home, staying at her estate for a time.\nLilian spent that brief, warm period with\nthe people she loved, just as she dreamed.\nBut in Lilian's heart, she knew there were\nstill people in the world needing a savior.\nSo Lilian said farewell through her tears\nas {AvatarName} set out on a journey,\nwith the promise that they would meet\nagain. "Can't be too sad about it," she would\nlater say. "I mean, how many people can say\nthey have the Promised One's love?"
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Lys_001: Lysander saw {AvatarName} off on their\njourney of salvation, praying for bright\nfutures for them both. He later returned to\nSaramis and continued to serve diligently.\nIn time, he rose to the position of chancellor,\nbecoming a leader to the people. Though he\nwas proud of this duty, he still recalled his\ndays with the Promised One. When he\nheard a report of a figure in white, he left\nto give chase, thinking of all that went\nunsaid between them. At last, Lysander was\nreunited with the one he longed for.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Buc_001: Having fulfilled his role, Buccar chose to\nspend the rest of his life with one he truly\nloved, {AvatarName}. He felt the same\nsense of duty to them as to Guillermo, his\nprevious lord. Buccar accompanied\n{AvatarName} on their journey of\nsalvation and was prepared to sacrifice\nhimself to protect them whenever necessary.\nHe was consistently chastised for this, but\nalways remained proud and laughed off the\nscoldings. Those who knew him before were\nsurprised to see how content he seemed.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Sci_001: Though the war in Dagda had ended,\nlingering turmoil smoldered throughout the\nland. {CapitalizeNextLetter}{AvatarName} set out to quell it,\nwith Sirocco following breezily in their\nwake. He watched over {AvatarName}\nlike a weather vane, heedlessly intervening\nwhenever they met with danger. Sirocco\nonce remarked with a laugh that, while he\nmay be the wind, the Promised One was\nthe sail that caught him. But then he grew\nserious and vowed to spend the rest of his\nlife by their side.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Moo_001: Mu decided to join {AvatarName}'s quest\nto aid those who were suffering. The young\nwoman learned much from her time fighting\nalongside them. She would eventually put\nthe knowledge gained during that journey\nto use in making many crucial discoveries\nabout medicinal plants. Some years later,\nshe revolutionized the field of non-magical\nbotany. History would remember Mu as the\nmother of Dagdan medicine.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Mic_001: Despite Balor's demise, chaos lingered\nthroughout the land. In order to quell it,\n{AvatarName} set out on a journey of\nsalvation. Mikaela insisted on coming along\nand, true to her word, fought by their side\nfor the sake of the world. Though Mikaela\nwas single-minded and stubborn, it was said\nthat {AvatarName} was not displeased\nwith their time together. "Fighting's all I'm\ngood for, but if we can fight for a better\nworld, I'll take it," said Mikaela with\ngratitude to her beloved partner.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Oly_001: Having relinquished the title Rose of Caelus,\nOlympia began to make a name for herself\nonstage as a singer. From their seat in the\nfront row, {AvatarName} watched as\nOlympia sang her heart out day after day.\nAfter each performance, {AvatarName}\nwould offer astute feedback, which often left\nOlympia speechless. The songstress kept\nimproving, her popularity in Dagsion\ngrowing by the day, and years later she was\nknown far and wide as the best singer in\nall of Dagda.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Naz_001: With little time left, Nezha decided to\nembark on a grueling journey of training,\ntrue to his nature. {CapitalizeNextLetter}{AvatarName} chose\nto accompany him. Nezha's short temper\noften led to unnecessary fights between\nthem, but their travels were otherwise lively\nand fulfilling. True to his word, Nezha never\nwavered from his principles and devoted\nhimself fully to honing his skills. In the end,\nas he promised, he passed away peacefully\nin {AvatarName}'s presence.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Sar_001: Sha Lan set out with {AvatarName},\nwho would save people without asking\nanything in return. She devoted herself\ndeeply to them along the way. Tales of the\nPromised One and their companion\nflourished across Dagda. Decades passed,\nSha Lan grew old, and the moment of her\nparting with {AvatarName} finally\narrived. She bade farewell to the one she\nloved most, cursing her lack of a Heart Core.\nThey shared an emotional embrace as she\nsaid, "You truly gave my life meaning."
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Dai_001: Dadao and {AvatarName} set out on a\njourney together, but Dadao's persistent\nhabit of hitting on women caused the two\nof them trouble wherever they went, giving\n{AvatarName} headaches. Still, Dadao\nhad deep respect for {AvatarName},\nwho understood him well. Thirty years later,\nas his strength faded, Dadao decided to end\nhis journey. Hoping that someone would\nsomeday carry on his work of helping the\nPromised One, Dadao watched the figure\nin white fade into the distance.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Hal_001: Halvin entertained crowds by day and\nstudied agriculture at night at the temple\narchives. After buying land on the outskirts\nof Dagsion, she began testing cultivation\nmethods. Within a few years, her efforts\nbegan to pay off, bringing abundant\nharvests. As her methods became widely\nknown, they improved the standard of\nliving for all the land. True to her vow,\nHalvin continued to wait for the day\n{AvatarName} returned to Dagsion,\noften saying, "Maybe it'll be tomorrow."
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Guj_001: After the great battle for the future of\nhumankind, order returned to the world,\nthough chaos was not entirely vanquished.\nGuzran was no different than before, living\nin Dagsion while boasting of his heroic\nexploits, some of which were almost true.\nMeanwhile, {AvatarName} continued\njourneying to quell the chaos across the\nland, but they always made sure to visit\nGuzran whenever they were in Dagsion.\nThe two were often seen making toasts and\ncelebrating until dawn.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Yan_001: Though the battle with Balor was over, the\nland was far from stable. {CapitalizeNextLetter}{AvatarName}\nset out on a journey to help those suffering\nacross Dagda. Yang Jie undertook a similar\nmission, deciding to head in the opposite\ndirection. On the morning they departed,\nYang Jie and {AvatarName} confirmed\nthat, though their paths were different, their\ngoals were the same, and promised they\nwould meet again someday. There are many\nstories of the two individually, but no record\nof them ever meeting again.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Iio_001: Io returned to Arago to fight for peace in his\nhomeland, which was still in the grip of the\npostwar chaos. Before he knew it, he had\nbecome the ideal knight he always hoped to\nbe, earning the respect of those around\nhim—though he himself was uncomfortable\nwith such treatment. Decades later, Io was\nvisited by a shining figure while bedridden\nwith illness. "Isn't it a little late for you to\nfeel lonely?" he asked resentfully, but the\njoy in his eyes belied his words. Still,\n{AvatarName} nodded apologetically.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Pep_001: Peppe returned to Brigid and busied himself\nwith his rule. He reinforced relations with\nthe nations of Dagda, despite the turmoil\nthere, and made a point to visit the land\nperiodically in person. To his vassals' shock,\nhe showed great personal growth after the\ngreat war. Years later, {AvatarName}\nvisited Brigid during their journey of\nsalvation, where Peppe was waiting to fulfill\nhis promise. The young king was overjoyed\nto see them and held a national celebration\nin honor of the Promised One's arrival.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Noc_001: Noctula worked hard on reconstructing\nDagsion, as she told {AvatarName} she\nwould. She wanted to restore the city to its\nformer glory for when {AvatarName}\nwould eventually visit during their travels.\nAs Noctula led the effort, more and more\nvolunteers signed on with the project. By the\ntime she reached middle age, Dagsion was\nmore bustling than it had ever been. When\nshe heard a figure in white had arrived,\nNoctula rushed to greet them, saying,\n"Luminous One! I gave it all I had!"
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Sop_001: Sofia worked proactively with the temples\nto build a shrine to Solel. On top of her\nheroism in the Underworld War, Sofia\nwas well liked by all for her personality.\nTen years later, she rose to the rank of\nhigh priest of the restored temple of\nSolel. She was very old by the time of her\nreunion with the Promised One, but she was\nsatisfied to have achieved her lifelong\ndream. {CapitalizeNextLetter}{AvatarName} had complicated\nfeelings about the shrine, but they\ncongratulated her on the achievement.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Cat_001: Catania set out with {AvatarName} to\nsave a world still in chaos. Though she\ninsisted it was all to win glory for herself,\n{AvatarName} knew that deep down\nCatania needed to do good. They set right\nmany wrongs, and the people's appreciation\ngreatly boosted her self-esteem. Catania and\n{AvatarName} had a merry journey, and\ntheir trust in each other led to remarkable\nfeats, making them local legends wherever\nthey went. "I've finally become the person\nI wanted to be," she sighed.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Ned_001: Together with {AvatarName}, Nydine\nswept away the turmoil lingering in the land\nof Dagda, saving the oppressed and\nsuffering. Their journey had no agreed-upon\nend, and Nydine learned a great many\nthings as she lent her martial arts skills\nto {AvatarName}. Eventually, she\nbelieved she had gained that which she\nthirsted for, and felt satisfied. Later legends\ntold in Dagda of the Promised One always\nmentioned Nydine, the noble warrior\ndisciple who accompanied them.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Zac_001: {CapitalizeNextLetter}{AvatarName} brought along a reluctant\nZarcone on their journey of salvation.\nThough Zarcone was frequently tempted to\nwicked deeds, each time he was thwarted\nand urged to reflect deeply on his actions.\nAs time passed, Zarcone changed little by\nlittle, and he began to find joy in the\ngratitude of others. Before long, he came to\nlove {AvatarName} with all his heart,\nand he became a respected disciple of the\nPromised One. The unusual pair continued\nto journey together for many years.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Maj_001: Majide spent his days protecting the\npeace in Dagsion in order to realize his\ndream of becoming the city's ruler. Despite\nworking tirelessly, he never made inroads\nto becoming a ruler, though he eventually\nfound joy in the people's gratitude. Ten\nyears later, {AvatarName} returned to\nDagsion for the first time in a while and\nsaw Majide in charge of the city's security.\nTheir eyes met, he sniffled with\nembarrassment, and he said, "What are you\nlooking at? You took your sweet time!"
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Ven_001: {CapitalizeNextLetter}{AvatarName} set out on a journey of\nsalvation, letting the road take them where\nit would. Benditz insisted on coming along,\ndevoting himself in his own way to his\nbeloved Promised One. Though Benditz\nnever did achieve his lifelong dream of\nbecoming a general, he was said to be\nsurprisingly content. In the memoirs Benditz\npenned in his later years, he wrote that their\ntravels together were spirited, and that the\nPromised One relied on him thoroughly in\nall things.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Ini_001: After the battle for the fate of the world,\nInyoni returned to her family and used her\nabilities for the benefit of others, keeping\nan altruistic attitude throughout the rest of\nher life. In years of lean harvest, they shared\nthe food they hunted. If bandits attacked a\nvillage, she went to fight them off. She had\nmany suitors, but never agreed to marriage\nno matter how favorable the terms. Village\nrecords contain several instances of a\nfigure clad all in white visiting Inyoni.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Jas_001: Jasmine decided to go back to her home of\nBrigid on {AvatarName}'s advice.\nUpon her return, Brigid's monarch selected\nher as a personal bodyguard, on the strength\nof her renown as a hero of the Underworld\nWar. As she lived out a fulfilling life there,\nevery few years a mysterious figure in white\nwould visit, and she would put everything\naside to be with them. The joyful time they\nspent together was recounted briefly in a\nbook covering daily life within the palace.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Ale_001: When Alexandra returned to her home, she\nused the evidence her parents left to prove\nher uncle's wrongdoings to the temples.\nHis confiscated assets went toward building\na shelter for those who had no place to go.\nIn recognition of her altruism, Jurah\nbestowed on her a clan name, and her\nhouse flourished thereafter. Alexandra\nserved Jurah for many years, with\n{AvatarName} always at her side in\nsupport. Some unverified records suggest\nthe two had children together.
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Cle_001: 
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Mys_001: 
MID_END_Pair_Ism_Kou_001: Hong Hua departed with {AvatarName}\non a journey of atonement to save all those\nstill suffering. Though she claimed it was\nonly for her own sake, she worked with\n{AvatarName} to better people's lives,\ndeepening their trust in each other along\nthe way. The pair's journey would not end\nuntil their Heart Cores gave out, and even\nHong Hua could not know when that time\nmight come. As time passed, the legend of\na pair of saviors spread all over the world,\neven beyond the borders of Dagda.
MID_END_Pair_Kai_Seo_001: After the war, Theodora was a powerful\nleader, stabilizing Saramis ahead of the\nother nations before announcing her\nengagement to Cai. The people were excited\nby the prospect of a marriage between two\nheroes of the Underworld War and planned\na festival lasting over a month to celebrate\nthe pair. Cai supported Theodora behind the\nscenes and, when necessary, in battle—\nensuring not only victory but the people's\ntrust. Cai came to be a figure just as\nbeloved as Theodora.
MID_END_Pair_Kai_Led_001: On orders from Jurah, who assumed the\nthrone of Divine Sovereign, Cai was made\na general of the Dagdan Empire. He worked\nhard to quell the chaos remaining in the\nland, and Leda was at his side for it all as\nhis wife. Her iron will helped to make up for\nCai's moments of indecision, and together\nthey worked for peace until death separated\nthem. History records that, though Leda\nwould sometimes look on her husband's\nyouthful face with sadness, she lived an\noverall contented life.
MID_END_Pair_Kai_Tia_001: Cai proposed to Tialla and she joyfully\naccepted. The two of them began their new\nlife in a rental home in Dagsion. Shortly\nafterward, Cai entered government service\nin response to the empire's dire need,\nworking hard as a general to quell the chaos\nin each kingdom. Tialla meanwhile fulfilled\nher dream of reading the wealth of books in\nthe temples as a priest. At long last, they\nwere blessed with a child, and Cai had the\nnormal family he longed for. Aurora would\nsometimes visit, and life seemed perfect.
MID_END_Pair_Kai_Hur_001: Ultand continued to serve Aurora as the\ngoddess shifted to working on behalf of the\npeople. She reunited with Cai when he\nvisited the temple to propose to her—after\nall, he already thought of her as family.\nCai became a general of the empire, while\nUltand retired from the temples to take care\nof her new family. Counting the four\nchildren they had together, their household\nof six was a joyous one.
MID_END_Pair_Kai_Esm_001: Esmeralda concealed her identity as a hero\nof the Underworld War and moved to a\nsmall harbor town, making ends meet as a\nfisher. After settling into her new life,\nshe happened to reunite with Cai when\nhe visited. Seeing kindred spirits in each\nother, the two began to live together. Cai\nlearned the ropes of fishing from Esmeralda,\nand before they knew it, they'd hauled up\nsome of the largest fish in the Lir Sea.\nTheir names rang out anew as legendary\nfishers throughout Dagda.
MID_END_Pair_Kai_Ale_001: The newly minted General Cai reunited\nwith Alexandra on the battlefield. The two\nhad a whirlwind romance, resulting in a\ntemple wedding after only a year. It was the\nfirst time Alexandra learned of Cai's mother,\nnearly causing her to faint. But she quickly\nbefriended Aurora, as if they were a natural\nduo, and was welcomed into the family\nalong with Bucephalus. One historian tells\nof how the two fought side by side for years\nafterward in hopes of bringing peace back\nto the land.
MID_END_Pair_Bel_Max_001: Bertrand strove to realize his vision for the\nDagdan Alliance. Maxim not only served as\nhis aide, but also his tailor, and had final\nsay over what Bertrand wore to diplomatic\naffairs. The many innovative outfits he\ncreated for the king became fashionable\nand widely imitated. In later histories of\nDagda, it was written that King Bertrand\nwas always impeccably dressed due to\nMaxim's influence. All scholars of the era\nagree on this point.
MID_END_Pair_Bel_Gol_001: Bertrand worked day and night to realize his\nplan for the Dagdan Alliance. At his side\nwas Goliath, always there to support him\nwholeheartedly. Though Bertrand made\nmany enemies, some of whom wished death\nupon him, most cowered at the sight of\nGoliath and reconsidered their plans. Years\nlater, Goliath died a hero as he covered\nBertrand's escape in a desperate battle.\nDeeply saddened, Bertrand had a huge tomb\nbuilt for his large friend and told his aides to\nbury him with Goliath when his time came.
MID_END_Pair_Bel_Gat_001: Bertrand began working on his plan for the\nDagdan Alliance as he waited for peace to\nreturn to Brezarant. Gaitz was always at his\nside in this as his closest aide. The Alliance\nlater sent envoys to the eastern nations\nof Rama, Normalia, and Sai, and these\nexpeditions met with great success. Many\nbelieved that Gaitz's deft diplomatic touch\nwas a major factor in these endeavors.
MID_END_Pair_Bel_Dan_001: Bertrand began working on his plan for the\nDagdan Alliance as he waited for peace to\nreturn to Brezarant. Dante served as his\nscribe, recording all of his deeds in detail,\nbut never held back her passionate rhetoric\nwhen it came to chiding her husband. Both\nhe and those around him found satisfaction\nto know she was dedicated to holding him\naccountable. Later in life, Dante published\nThe Eternal Bloodaxe, which she spent\nhalf her life writing. In time, it would be\nrecognized as the apex of Dagdan literature.
MID_END_Pair_Bel_Asw_001: After the war, Bertrand announced his\nlong-held plan for the Dagdan Alliance.\nArago was quick to sign on, forming a huge\nnation in the western reaches that would\nimpose new order on the land. When\nharmony began to return to Dagda, Bertrand\nannounced his marriage to Aswan. The\npeople turned out in droves to congratulate\nthe pair, whose lives seemed destined to\nintermingle. It was common for authors to\nwrite plays based on them, many of which\nwere hailed as classics by later generations.
MID_END_Pair_Dit_Bel_001: Bertrand gained support from other nations \nto realize his plan for the Dagdan Alliance,\nexpanding his power as a unifying king.\nWhile Bertrand was seen as the rightful\nsuccessor to the authority of the Dagdan\nEmpire, Dietrich always lurked nearby,\nplotting to kill him—though he would never\nallow anyone else to do so. Whenever he\nuncovered an assassination scheme, he\nwould invariably slaughter all involved.\nThus did the world's most fearsome killer\nbecome the king's most reliable guardian.
MID_END_Pair_Dit_Led_001: Dietrich continued to wander Dagda in\nsearch of chaos to combat, and Leda went\nwith him. She claimed they happened to be\nheading in the same direction, but those\nwho saw them together said they got along\nquite well. The beautiful swordsman and\nthe legendary musician attracted attention\nwherever they went. They had a captivating\npresence but also struck fear in the hearts\nof those who saw them. The two departed\nDagda for some faraway land, and their\nwhereabouts thereafter remain unclear.
MID_END_Pair_Dit_Fab_001: Even after Balor's defeat, Dietrich roamed\nthe land of Dagda for still more formidable\nopponents. His blood-soaked exploits are too\nmany to enumerate, but Fabio was there for\nall of them. After a hundred years, an\nelderly Dietrich was met with an elite force\nof two thousand knights bent on striking\nhim down. Seeing that death was upon him,\nhe smiled. Though Dietrich bade him to\nreturn to Fódlan, Fabio stayed at his side to\nmeet a glorious end alongside Dietrich. The\nrecords of them say nothing further.
MID_END_Pair_Dit_Esm_001: Esmeralda moved to a little harbor town,\npurchasing a small boat with the spoils of\nwar, and made ends meet by fishing. Going\ninto town to sell fish, she happened to\nreunite with a passing Dietrich. As they\ntalked, they decided to go fishing, and\nhauled up a monster of a fish after a bitter\nstruggle. Dietrich's curiosity was piqued by\nthis battle with mighty nature, and he began\nto accompany her on her fishing trips. They\nstayed together for 10 years afterward, and\nin that time Esmeralda bore two children.
MID_END_Pair_Dit_Mic_001: Though the great battle was over, Dietrich's\nthirst was yet unslaked, so he roamed the\nland in search of new and powerful foes.\nUnwilling to abandon him, Mikaela went\nalong, and on one occasion they exhibited\nexcellent harmony in combat. Dietrich was\nnever one to listen to others' opinions, but\nthe records suggest he followed Mikaela's\nadvice diligently. They continued traveling\nfor some 20 years before Mikaela grew\nold and retired from combat. Many tales of\ntheir exploits still circulate across Dagda.
MID_END_Pair_Dit_Hal_001: Even after the war, Dietrich wandered the\nland of Dagda in search of strong foes,\nbut he collapsed after receiving a serious\ninjury in battle. Halvin happened to be on\nthe scene, and although she was frightened\nof him, she couldn't leave him to die, and\ndressed his wounds. Once he had healed,\nDietrich set off again, promising that if his\nthirst was ever sated, he would return to\nHalvin. But she was unsatisfied with letting\nhim go alone and insisted on accompanying\nDietrich on his travels.
MID_END_Pair_Tal_Urs_001: One day, Talimun gathered a crowd in\nDagsion to announce his marriage to Ursula.\nTheir wedding guests were treated to\ndelicacies from land and sea, as well as\nexotic liquors. Though this development\nsurprised those close to the couple, it was\nnot altogether unexpected. The guests\ncongratulated the embarrassed Talimun and\nsmiling Ursula on their future together. The\ntwo continued as coworkers despite their\nmarriage, and their five children knew\nTalimun as both loving and strict.
MID_END_Pair_Tal_Sim_001: Simon stayed with the Vandahl Trading\nCompany, spending his days going on jobs\nat Talimun's request—though they weren't\nprecisely friends. About 20 years later, while\nTalimun was off on a long "vacation," the\nZaratan was attacked by pirates. Simon led\nthe crew in fending them off, but perished\nfrom wounds sustained in the attack. When\nTalimun discovered this upon returning\nfrom vacation, his manager's log noted his\nimmense grief.
MID_END_Pair_Tal_Lou_001: Talimun abruptly announced his marriage to\nLudia, throwing the Vandahl Trading\nCompany into an uproar. Ludia saw the\nproposal as a chance for her future husband\nto reconcile with her father. She was right,\nand both families prospered as a result.\nLudia continued her work for the company\nand died at the young age of 45, but the\nbook she wrote about life with her eccentric\nhusband persisted after her death. Anytime\nTalimun spoke of his wife, he would smile\nsadly, saying, "She was too good to pass up."
MID_END_Pair_Tal_Fia_001: Talimun made a grand announcement of his\nmarriage to Fianna. Though they kept her\nidentity secret, later scholars noted the\nsuspiciously preferential treatment from\nArago shortly afterward. Fianna continued\nto work for the Vandahl Trading Company,\npassing away about 30 years later. Several\nsources recorded Fianna's bliss at having her\nbeloved husband all to herself. They also\nnoted Talimun's state after her death and\nwrote of how seriously his bereavement for\nhis beloved wife affected him.
MID_END_Pair_Tal_Mic_001: Talimun proposed to Mikaela, saying, "I bet\nyou never thought you'd bag the richest man\nin Dagda." Mikaela was confused by this\nproposal but came to accept his brand of\nlove. She decided to remarry, and the two\nfound wedded bliss together. As a company\nwarrior, Mikaela trained the young recruits,\nturning Vandahl's security into a force that\nbandits feared going up against at the risk of\ntheir lives. Mikaela also spent a great deal\nof time ensuring their shared rooms were\nclean, which Talimun found distracting.
MID_END_Pair_Orh_Die_001: After the war, Orchel returned to Credna's\ntemple with Diego. At Orchel's insistence,\nher true identity was kept a secret. Though\nlife returned to normal, Diego's experiences\nof war softened him, and he threw himself\ninto temple work. Diego served Orchel\nfaithfully until his death at the age of 77,\neventually rising to the rank of lead priest,\njust as Orchel once was. Throughout his life,\nhis deep reverence for her never wavered.
MID_END_Pair_Orh_Set_001: Seteth took up a corner in Credna's temple\nand devoted himself to transcribing the vast\namount of texts there. His aim was to report\nall he had experienced in Dagda to his\ncomrades waiting at the Church of Seiros.\nOrchel would often visit, asking about the\nstate of Fódlan, and told him stories of the\nancient Nabateans from her memories.\nThrough these exchanges, Seteth deepened\nhis understanding of history. Even after\nreturning to Fódlan, he occasionally recalled\nthe beautiful yet star-crossed goddess.
MID_END_Pair_Orh_Nin_001: When Orchel returned to Credna's main\ntemple, she resumed her former life. Ninae's\nrequest to Archpriest Gephma was granted,\nand she was transferred from the branch\ntemple in Dagsion, officially becoming\nOrchel's attendant vulkan. Ninae adored\nthe priest as if she were her own mother, to\nwhich Orchel responded as best she could.\nWhile it was unusual for a vulkan to serve\na mere lead priest, the two had a certain\neasy understanding that made the\narrangement seem natural.
MID_END_Pair_Seo_Bel_001: With the Dagdan Empire weakened by the\nchaos of Balor, Bertrand announced the\nDagdan Alliance, with himself at the head.\nArago was the first to join, followed by other\npowerful allies. Queen Theodora brought\nSaramis into the alliance through her\nwedding with Bertrand. Though chaos still\nreigned over the land of Dagda, their new\nwave of harmony based on Bertrand's ideals\nwas poised to take its place.
MID_END_Pair_Seo_Tal_001: Theodora happily united with Talimun,\nbringing unprecedented growth to both\nSaramis and the Vandahl Trading Company.\nA dozen years later, she lent Saraminian\nexpertise to building the huge, Vandahl-\nfunded ship Breandán. Talimun sailed it\nfrom Alecto for the western lands but\ndisappeared along the way and never\nreturned. Poets began to tell tales of his life\non the new continent, including an absurd\nyarn where he became king at the end of\none of his adventures.
MID_END_Pair_Seo_Anh_001: When the chaos within her kingdom began\nto abate, Theodora was visited by Anatolia,\nwho had become queen of the ancient\nkingdom of Solomon. The two nations with\na shared ancestry forged diplomatic ties.\nSaramis traded minerals such as iron ore,\njewels, and gold for rare produce from\nSolomon, greatly contributing to Saramis's\ndevelopment. Several years later, Theodora\ngave birth to a son and named him Ararat.\nThe people joyously greeted the heir, but the\nfather's name was strangely never revealed.
MID_END_Pair_Seo_Bon_001: Theodora revealed Yu Phas's true intentions\nto her people and repealed the ordinance\nagainst writing, launching a dedicated\neducational institute in Saramis. Many\nclung to the ancient tradition, but Theodora\npersevered in persuading them. Against that\nbackground, Theodora announced her\nengagement to Bonaventure. Though the\npeople were surprised, they celebrated the\nmarriage. The pair, whose bond was beyond\nqueen and retainer, had two children,\nheralding greater things ahead for Saramis.
MID_END_Pair_Seo_Tob_001: When things in Saramis finally settled, it\ncame as a surprise when Theodora chose\nTobias for her husband. The announcement\ncaused a stir, but few were more astonished\nthan Tobias. "I have given it much thought\nand concluded that you are my best match,"\nshe said. "Do not make me repeat myself."\nBut Tobias sensed her sincerity and\naccepted her love. Becoming his queen's\nhusband changed his personality not at all,\nand he remained beloved throughout the\nkingdom.
MID_END_Pair_Seo_Lys_001: Lysander worked hard to quell the tumult\nthat lingered after the war. He was praised\nfor his loyalty to his queen and his\nconsiderate nature. After years of service,\nhe was appointed as a high commander.\nLysander offered sound advice even in tense\nsituations, and proactively debated ideas\nwith Theodora. One day she asked him if\nhe had any interest in her as a companion.\nHe humbly accepted the role as her\nhusband. But his principles never bended,\nand he was strict yet fair to the last.
MID_END_Pair_Led_Bel_001: Bertrand, who continued work on realizing\nhis dream, announced his engagement to\nnone other than Leda. Putting her in a\nposition of easy access to the king caused an\nuproar in Bertrand's court, but despite these\nfears, Leda was always considerate of her\nhusband and did her best to support him.\nWhen anyone questioned her intentions,\nLeda grew sulky and gave vague answers.\nHistorians later believed this was because\nshe realized that Bertrand was always the\nonly one for her.
MID_END_Pair_Led_Buc_001: Leda decided to rebuild House Cohendia in\nCydonia and protect that which her father\nheld dear. This decision may have stemmed\nfrom a desire to grant her beloved Buccar's\nwish. Leda invested her earnings from the\nwar and treasure provided by Kalla toward\nrebuilding both her house and Kassite, and\nBuccar devoted himself to aiding her. With\nthe support of the people, House Cohendia\nwas eventually restored. For his part, Buccar\nremained unwaveringly loyal to Leda until\nhis final moments.
MID_END_Pair_Led_Sci_001: After the war, Sirocco continued to serve\nKalla as before, with one change: Leda\nbegan working alongside him. They\ninfiltrated many places and uncovered\nmany injustices, always having each other's\nbacks as the perfect partners. Years later,\nthey left Kalla's temple to wander Dagda as\ntraveling bards, doing what they could\nto right wrongs wherever they went. When\nSirocco dryly remarked that their lifestyle\nwasn't so different from what they left\nbehind, Leda gave him a mischievous grin.
MID_END_Pair_Led_Moo_001: Mu, who developed a hidden talent after\nlearning to play a variety of instruments, set\nout on a journey to find Leda, who had\nvanished from Kalla's temple. Mu's gentle\nmusic put her listeners at ease, making her\na popular performer in taverns. The trail of\nrumors finally led her to Leda, and Mu\nconfessed her true feelings for her. Leda\napologized to Mu, reciprocated her feelings,\nand promised to spend time with Mu as her\npartner. Thus did the two musicians begin\na new legend in Dagda.
MID_END_Pair_Led_Oly_001: After the battle with Balor, Leda shut\nObsidian away in Kalla's temple and set off\non a journey to mourn those whose lives she\ntook while bringing closure to her emotions\nregarding Bertrand. It was also a way for\nher own heart to heal after it was strained\nto its limits. Olympia accompanied Leda on\nher quest, remaining constantly at her side.\nThus, many anecdotes of the beautiful and\nspirited Roses arose all across Dagda. Since\nboth were extremely poor cooks, they took\nall of their meals at restaurants.
MID_END_Pair_Anh_Naz_001: Nezha remained in Bilqis with Anatolia,\ndedicating himself to the construction of\nTiamat. Only a few years later, he began to\nrapidly age. Though offered the option of\ncryogenic sleep until a new Heart Core\ncould be transplanted, Nezha chose to live\nout his life, and Anatolia respected his\nchoice. In his final moments, Nezha\nexpressed his gratitude to Anatolia and\napologized that he couldn't stay with her\nlonger. Anatolia thanked him too before\nquietly witnessing his end.
MID_END_Pair_Anh_Sar_001: Sha Lan chose to remain in Bilqis with\nAnatolia. The two were like close sisters,\nwith Sha Lan eventually becoming\nchancellor of Solomon. She assisted with\nroutine affairs, as well as matters of trade,\ndiplomacy, and governance. Her keen\ninsight into what Anatolia's pure heart\nsometimes overlooked earned her a\nreputation as a formidable presence beside\nthe Forbidden Queen, especially among\nthose who sought to profit from exploiting\nthe mysterious kingdom of Solomon.
MID_END_Pair_Anh_Dai_001: Anatolia led the construction of Tiamat\ntoward its completion, while Dadao\nstayed in the Canopy City as her assistant.\nAlthough blueprints and documentation\nremained, the scarcity of key materials and\nthe loss of crucial equipment made progress\nchallenging. But Dadao's talents were\nuniquely suited for rising to this challenge.\nHe passed away at the age of 77, but\nNicaula's records showed that his efforts\nshortened the process of Tiamat's\nconstruction by about a hundred years.
MID_END_Pair_Anh_Hal_001: Halvin chose to remain in Bilqis with\nAnatolia. There, she witnessed the\nconstruction of Tiamat, an achievement\nthat would shape the next two hundred\nyears of human history. Anatolia asked\nHalvin to take on the important role of\nenvoy to the outside world. Though it was\na daunting responsibility, Halvin rose to the\nchallenge. As a diplomat for Solomon, she\neased tensions and exceeded expectations,\nmaking a significant contribution as only\nshe could.
MID_END_Pair_Tia_Pet_001: Known for his preeminent bow skill, Peter\ntook up residence in Dagsion and devoted\nhimself to training a new generation. His\ndeeds never became legend, but he was\ncontent with his life. At some point, Tialla,\nwho had attained her dream of serving the\ntemples, moved in with him. Though their\nmarriage had its ups and downs, the two\nloved each other dearly, and passed away\nwithin a year of each other as if destined.
MID_END_Pair_Tia_Bon_001: Tialla lived on Bonaventure's large estate to\nwork on the history of Saramis, visiting the\npalace daily to collect knowledge that had\nbeen passed down through the oral\ntradition. Though people gave her odd looks\nat first, her earnestness slowly won them\nover. Bonaventure watched it all with\nsatisfaction. After tenaciously checking and\nediting her research, Tialla completed the\nhistory of Saramis 10 years later. That was\nwhen Bonaventure told Tialla of his intent\nto bequeath all he owned to her.
MID_END_Pair_Pet_Hur_001: With Aurora resolved to keep her position\nand lead the people as a deity, Ultand\nreturned to the branch temple in Dagsion to\nattend her. One day at market, she ran into\nPeter, who had wound up as a farmer on the\noutskirts of Dagsion. As they reminisced\nabout old times, they grew closer, until\nUltand introduced Peter to her family. After\na period of courtship, they married and built\na happy household of their own. Peter was\nas timid as ever, but Ultand's force of will\nsaw the pair through thick and thin.
MID_END_Pair_Pet_Moo_001: Peter proposed to Mu, who gladly accepted.\nAfter sharing the news with their parents,\nthey moved to Ribeira to live an ordinary\nbut happy life. While helping Peter on the\nfarm, Mu would pick medicinal herbs from\nthe nearby fields for her experimental\nmedicines, which Peter volunteered to test.\nTwenty years later, Mu compiled her\nfindings into a book, which became a\nmust-have for every household in Dagda.
MID_END_Pair_Hur_Gol_001: Goliath returned to his daily life as a\ngladiator. Though he still played the part of\na heel, everyone cheered him as a hero.\nOne day, he sustained a terrible injury,\nlingering at the border of life and death for\na week. Ultand had been in the audience\nand felt duty bound to care for him. Goliath\nwas deeply moved and proposed to Ultand,\nhaving already harbored secret feelings for\nher. Years passed and Goliath became a\nlegend in the arena—thanks largely to his\nspouse's support from the sidelines.
MID_END_Pair_Max_Dan_001: Dante resumed her tireless work as a\nplaywright, with Maxim supporting her as\nher assistant. A year later, Dante debuted\na new play called The Infernal Clown,\nstarring Maxim as himself in the lead role.\nThis marked the start of Maxim's new life\nas an actor. Though he still had doubts\nwhether he or Jester was the real person,\nit encouraged him to hear from Dante that\nshe loved both sides of him equally.
MID_END_Pair_Max_Hal_001: After the final battle, Halvin began her new\nlife traveling across Dagda with Maxim as\nthey put on street performances. They\nentertained crowds in any village they\nvisited, but whenever they heard of bandits\ntroubling the local folk, they put a forceful\nstop to the problem. Their life together was\nlike a tribute to Nasshim, Halvin's mentor\nwho lost his life protecting her, and the\ncircus troupe he led. Before they knew it,\nthey were known across Dagda as a duo of\nskilled performers who helped those in need.
MID_END_Pair_Gol_Dan_001: Goliath became a star gladiator in Dagsion,\nand Dante made a point to attend his every\nmatch. After one rousing victory, Goliath\nannounced that there was someone in the\naudience he'd always loved, and he wanted\nto use this moment to propose to her. Dante\nblushed fiercely, protesting his decision to\nask her in front of such a huge audience,\nbefore humbly accepting the proposal. The\nwhole audience burst into applause.
MID_END_Pair_Gol_Lor_001: Loretta decided to leave Credna's temple,\nwhere she worked since she was a young\ngirl, and took on mercenary work around\nDagda to help quell the lingering chaos.\nGoliath refused to leave her side, and the\nodd duo of the slender beauty and hulking\nbeast attracted attention—especially since\nboth were outspoken and opinionated.\nIn battle, however, they worked in perfect\nharmony, capable of handling any job, no\nmatter how difficult. It wasn't long before\nthey became famed throughout the land.
MID_END_Pair_Gol_Oly_001: Olympia visited Goliath, a gladiator in\nDagsion, to invite him as her bodyguard on\na journey to broaden her horizons and hone\nher talents. He eagerly accepted, and the\nsight of the giant accompanying the skilled\nperformer attracted even larger crowds to\nOlympia's performances. As the two\ntraveled together, their bond grew deeper\nuntil they wed. Olympia, of course,\ncontinued to perform.
MID_END_Pair_Gat_Dan_001: After seeing to internal Brezarant affairs,\nGaitz set off to the eastern land of Sai once\nmore. This time Dante accompanied him,\non the pretext of doing research. Gaitz\nintended to pursue the dream he had when\nhe was young, and the story Dante once\nspun for him became a prophecy. The two\nbecame close during their journey and wed\nsoon after returning home. People from all\nover Dagda came to Breston to celebrate the\nunusual union of a famed Brezarant general\nand a rare literary talent.
MID_END_Pair_Gat_Urs_001: Ursula accepted Gaitz's proposal, resigned\nfrom her position at Vandahl Trading, and\nmoved to Brezarant. The newly married\ncouple, both of whom appeared younger\nthan they were, got along better than they\nexpected. The journals of Gaitz's steward\nindicated they were considerate of one\nanother and had a very happy union.\nMarriage seemed to calm Gaitz, and he\nbegan to place more importance on the\ninternal affairs of his country than on his\npersonal martial development.
MID_END_Pair_Gat_Ale_001: Gaitz announced to his close friends that he\nwas taking Alexandra as his spouse. They\nwere surprised by this decision but gave\nhim their blessings nonetheless. After\nsettling her relationship with her uncle,\nAlexandra resigned as a knight of Jurah and\nmarried into Gaitz's family. Together they\nserved Brezarant faithfully. Alexandra kept\nher martial skills sharp and became famed\nfor generations in Brezarant for her bravery.
MID_END_Pair_Fab_Esm_001: Fabio continued exploring the land of\nDagda, driven less by his mission than by\nsheer curiosity. He always kept meticulous\nrecords of his discoveries. Esmeralda would\naccompany him, making herself useful until\nthe two felt like master and pupil. When\nEsmeralda grew old and infirm, Fabio cared\nfor her until her last breath. In those final\nmoments, Fabio, in a departure from his\nusual demeanor, expressed his gratitude in\na flood of emotion.
MID_END_Pair_Fab_Mic_001: Continuing the mercenary life even after the\nwar, Mikaela threw herself into battle after\nbattle. A job took her to a certain village\nwhere she reunited with Fabio, who also\nhappened to be there. Mikaela worried for\nhis health and offered to take care of him\nafter her mission was over. He accepted\nwithout a trace of his reflexive snideness.\nMikaela understood no more of Fabio's\nresearch than ever, but she supported him\nnevertheless. In gratitude, he remained in\nDagda until the end of her natural life.
MID_END_Pair_Esm_Die_001: Diego took it upon himself to lead the\nremnants of the Har Hali, who had lost\ntheir homeland. At his side was Esmeralda,\nwhose cheerful kindness quickly won the\npeople to his leadership. Though Diego was\na man of few words, Esmeralda helped him\nshape the Har Hali and the forest peoples\ninto a mighty force, united in reverence for\nthe goddess Yu Phas. Whether Diego truly\nwished to rule as their first king, however,\nremains a matter of debate among scholars.
MID_END_Pair_Esm_Lys_001: Esmeralda decided to buy a ship in Dagsion\nand make a living fishing there, but found\nthe lake to be an unsatisfactory fishing spot.\nJust when she began considering a move to\nthe sea, Lysander came to visit. Having\nbeen recently promoted, he made a serious\nproposal of marriage to Esmeralda. And so\nit was that Esmeralda moved to a coastal\ncity in Saramis to start a life with Lysander.\nEsmeralda's down-to-earth nature made her\npopular among the young Saramis warriors,\nwho adored her as a mother figure.
MID_END_Pair_Urs_Sim_001: While Ursula busied herself with her duties\nas manager of Vandahl Trading, Simon left\nthe company and returned to mercenary life.\nA few years later, when the two met again \non unrelated business, Simon was unusually\nsolemn with Ursula, saying, "I don't want to\nwork for the company, but I'd gladly accept\na long-term contract with you." In return, he\nasked that Ursula spend her life with him\nfor as long as he should live. Understanding\nfull well the nature of the proposal, Ursula\naccepted with a wry smile.
MID_END_Pair_Sim_Lou_001: The many hair-raising events they shared\nsparked a mutual attraction in Simon and\nLudia. When Ludia introduced Simon\nto her family, her father, Senghor, was\nenraged and took her back from Vandahl\nTrading. But later, when Senghor was in a\nbind, Ludia used what she learned from\nSimon to overcome it, changing her father's\nopinion of the man. A few years later, the\ntwo were happily married, and Simon used\nhis expertise to support Ludia when she was\nappointed as her father's successor.
MID_END_Pair_Sim_Fia_001: After many shared life experiences, Simon\nand Fianna decided to become partners.\nSimon settled in at Vandahl Trading due to\nFianna's wish that he never leave her sight.\nA few years later, they were blessed with a\nchild. Simon's love of fighting never waned,\nbut Fianna's influence led him to grow more\ncareful and less interested in womanizing.\nSimon's loving wife served spicy food at\nleast once a week, and his screams could\nsometimes be heard from their apartment.
MID_END_Pair_Sim_Lil_001: After saving up, Lilian finally recovered her\nfamily estate. Despite this, she chose to\nreturn to the battlefield as a mercenary. \nShe and Simon spent a year forming their\nown company, which performed well\nenough to become famed throughout Dagda.\nSimon entrusted Lilian with managing their\nmoney, forming a solid financial foundation\nfor their troops. Before long, they were\nwidely known as the top mercenary\ncompany in all of Dagda.
MID_END_Pair_Lou_Fia_001: Ludia continued her studies while working\nat Vandahl Trading. Her tireless efforts\nfinally bore fruit when she was appointed\nmanager of the newly established Morfis\nbranch. It was a high honor within the\ncompany, but Ludia only accepted on the\ncondition that Fianna accompany her.\nFianna agreed and the two of them\nestablished themselves in Morfis. With the\ntwo talented women at the helm, the new\nMorfis branch of Vandahl Trading quickly\nbegan to generate tremendous sales.
MID_END_Pair_Lou_Buc_001: Ludia visited Buccar after he made his\nreport at Guillermo's grave. Her assigned\nbranch at the company was plagued by\npirates, and when searching for a trusted\ncomrade, her feelings for Buccar led her to\nchoose him. Buccar accepted, performing\nsurprisingly well as a company bodyguard.\nAs Ludia expressed her gratitude to him,\nshe revealed her true feelings. Buccar was\ninitially flustered, but Ludia's earnestness\nwon him over. The rest of the company\nshowered them with their congratulations.
MID_END_Pair_Fia_Lys_001: Lysander waited until the chaos in Saramis\nsubsided before announcing his marriage to\nFianna. She quit her job and moved to\nSaramis, using the opportunity to strengthen\nthe relationship between Vandahl and\nSaramis, with both parties reaping huge\nprofits. Lysander took his uncle's place as\nchancellor within 15 years, but those close\nto them knew that Fianna's influence from\nbehind the scenes was a major factor in\nhis success.
MID_END_Pair_Die_Lor_001: Loretta devoted herself daily to her priestly\ntraining at Credna's temple. Though she\nstruggled with her resolve to become a lead\npriest loved by the people, as Orchel had\nbeen, she remained determined. On seeing\nher efforts, Diego would show support, and\nthe trust between them grew stronger. In\ntime, they became life partners, and\nArchpriest Gephma watched over them.\nAs years passed, they both grew in esteem\nas priests in Credna's temple, dedicating\ntheir lives to serving the people.
MID_END_Pair_Die_Nin_001: With nowhere else to go, Diego was still\nserving at Credna's temple when Ninae\narrived, having been granted a request to\ntransfer to the main temple. Diego found\nsolace in her quiet presence and found\nhimself increasingly drawn to her purity.\nWhenever Diego and Ninae had a moment\nalone, perhaps while searching the nearby\nforest for missing people or returning lost\nanimals to their habitats, Diego would play\nhis flute and Ninae would listen, enraptured.
MID_END_Pair_Lor_Set_001: After the war, Seteth decided to leave the\nland of Dagda, but not before revealing his\nidentity to Loretta. He told her of his ties to\nthe Church of Seiros in Fódlan, and his\nreason for coming to Dagda. He spoke of\nhow lucky he was to meet Orchel and\nLoretta, and how fulfilled he'd felt in their\nyears together. Seteth encouraged Loretta\nto come to Fódlan someday, to which she\nnodded. Their bond transcended their age\nand nationalities. Loretta wrote to Seteth\nwith updates, and he would regularly reply.
MID_END_Pair_Set_Nin_001: To record all he had seen and heard in\nDagda, Seteth took a corner of the temple\nand wrote each day. Ninae would stop by to\nreview his drafts and point out any errors.\nHer remarkably accurate memory was\ninvaluable to Seteth, and when his history\nwas complete and he was ready to return to\nFódlan, he asked Ninae if she would come\nwith him. Curious about Seteth's daughter\nand the spirits in his homeland, Ninae\ngladly accepted and crossed the sea, bound\nfor Fódlan.
MID_END_Pair_Bon_Lil_001: Rumors spread like wildfire among the\nSaramis army that Bonaventure had found\na new wife. Seeking the truth, Chancellor\nKumos visited his old friend, where he\nfound an uneasy Bonaventure being well\ncared for by Lilian. Unable to sit by and\nwatch Bonaventure wither away alone, she\nhad barged in and made herself at home.\nOn seeing their sappy domestic life for\nhimself, Kumos left in a daze, but he did\nremember to send his old friend large\nquantities of fine wine to congratulate him.
MID_END_Pair_Tob_Lil_001: Just when the turmoil began to subside,\nrumors spread that Commander Tobias had\ngotten married. The surprised officers went\nto his home to find him living happily with\nLilian, who had decided to retire from the\narmy and care for their household. Possibly\nbecause he was so moved by this, Tobias\ncut back on drinking and showed a new\nsolemnity they'd never seen. The two of\nthem had several children, and many who\nknew Tobias envied him for managing to\nfind such a fine partner.
MID_END_Pair_Tob_Oly_001: After learning a new song from Tobias,\nOlympia began spending more time with\nhim. One day, Tobias sheepishly asked her\nto come with him to Saramis. When asked\nwhy, he told Olympia that he wanted to\nmarry her. After considering whether life\nin a foreign land would allow her to truly\nblossom, she ultimately accepted his offer.\nThe whole of Saramis was shocked to see\nCommander Tobias married to such a lovely\nwoman. In later years, Olympia became an\nimportant cultural figure within Saramis.
MID_END_Pair_Lil_Lys_001: Lysander's diligent service and military feats\nearned him a position as a high commander.\nHaving reached the milestone he set for\nhimself, he called upon Lilian to confess\nhis long-held feelings. Before he could even\nfinish, she heckled him, saying, "That took\nway longer than I thought." Nevertheless,\nshe agreed, and the two were wed. Though\nmarriage didn't change her, in public she\ncomported herself with dignity befitting a\ndaughter of a noble house, in honor of her\nhigh commander of a husband.
MID_END_Pair_Buc_Oly_001: Buccar was recognized by the temples in\nDagsion for his experience and took on the\nrole of mentor for younger generations, just\nas he once had. Olympia began making a\nhabit of visiting him whenever she could,\nto have a captive audience for her boasting\nand complaining. Whenever she stopped by,\nBuccar always laid out fine tea and baked\ngoods for her. Realizing that she found\ngreat comfort in his company, she asked if\nhe would remain always at her side, and\nhe vowed that he would.
MID_END_Pair_Sci_Moo_001: As a vulkan in Kalla's temple, Sirocco was\nall over Dagda. Mu, having become a priest,\nwent with him as his assistant—at the\nrequest of Kalla, who secretly saw the two\nof them as a good match. Though Sirocco\nwas a bit hesitant to have a partner who'd\ngrown so beautiful, he wasn't opposed to the\nidea. Three years later, Sirocco officially\nproposed to Mu, who accepted. However,\nshe strictly forbade Sirocco from sharing a\nbed with anyone but herself, even for work,\nshowing shrewd judgment on her part.
MID_END_Pair_Sci_Oly_001: As a vulkan in Kalla's temple, Sirocco\nwas all over Dagda. With his goddess's\nblessing, Olympia went with him. Though\nthe two seemed constantly at odds, they\nalways carried out their missions and were\nknown to be excellent partners both in\npublic and in private. Later, Olympia was\nnamed a vulkan of Kalla's in her own right\nand given the name Olympia the Cultivated.\nHer achievements alongside Syracusio of\nthe Silver Hail were among the most\ncolorful in Dagda's history.
MID_END_Pair_Sci_Sar_001: Sha Lan followed in Anatolia's footsteps,\nmaking a living in Dagsion as a fortune\nteller. She also took on the role of liaison\nwith Troy, proud of her work with Jiang\nto connect her kin scattered across Dagda.\nOne day, Sirocco surprised Sha Lan by\nvisiting her fortune-telling booth to ask that\nshe become his wife. She didn't answer him\ninitially, but his relentless enthusiasm\neventually won her over. Through their\nefforts, the divide between the temples and\nthe descendants of Nuwa at last came down.
MID_END_Pair_Mic_Sim_001: Even after the great war ended, minor\ndisputes continued to roil the land of Dagda.\nSimon's job as a hired blade led him to a\nfamiliar face: Mikaela, who came to realize\nthat mercenary work was her calling. The\ntwo hit it off and began working together,\nbecoming equal partners who relied on each\nother. The many dramatic stories of\nSky-Drum and Redblade became fodder\nfor bards for ages to come.
MID_END_Pair_Naz_Sar_001: Sha Lan decided to open the restaurant she\nhad dreamed of in Dagsion. As a hero of the\nUnderworld War and a master of traditional\nKunlun recipes, she gained widespread\nacclaim with her cooking. Before long,\nNezha drifted into her shop and started\nworking alongside her. When asked if he\nwas sure about this, he replied, "Whatever\nlets me spend the rest of my time with you."\nSha Lan decided then and there to stay with\nhim. The dish she created just for him was\na staple of her menu even after his passing.
MID_END_Pair_Naz_Hal_001: Even after the Underworld War, chaos\nthrived all across Dagda. In the midst of it\nall, Nezha set out on a journey of\nself-improvement, accompanied by Halvin.\nNezha was unsure about her joining him,\nsaying he had to train alone, but he\ngradually gave in and found himself relying\non her. The details of their journey, in\nwhich they worked together to overcome\nmany dangers, were recorded in the journals\nHalvin kept along the way.
MID_END_Pair_Sar_Dai_001: Sha Lan rented a building in Dagsion to\nopen her dream restaurant. Her traditional\nKunlun cuisine was very popular, but she\ndid worry about how to deal with unsavory\ncustomers. Dadao happened to be passing\nthrough as Sha Lan was harassed by a thug\nand helped her fend him off, leading to a\nreunion between the two. At Sha Lan's\nrequest, Dadao stayed at the restaurant,\nacting not only as security but also as head\nkitchen porter. With him on staff, Sha Lan's\nrestaurant became even more popular.
MID_END_Pair_Sar_Hal_001: Halvin bought land on the outskirts of\nDagsion to start her farm, though it didn't\ncome easily to her. Sha Lan occasionally\nvisited to teach her techniques from Kunlun,\nand gradually every problem was solved.\nAfter two years, her produce was good\nenough to sell. Sha Lan bought a vacant\nhouse not far from Halvin's farm, and their\nshared dream came true. Sha Lan's dishes\nmade with Halvin's produce were a hit, and\nher business prospered to the point that\nthere was always a line of customers.
MID_END_Pair_Dai_Hal_001: Using the funds she earned from battle,\nHalvin bought land in Iskandariya county\nand worked toward her dream of building a\nfamily farm. But the land was more barren\nthan she had hoped, leaving her at a loss\nuntil Dadao appeared and offered to help.\nHe crafted farming tools as needed to ease\nher burdens, bringing prosperity to the farm.\nHalvin decided to bring her family to join\nher, and soon afterward proposed to Dadao.\nThough caught off guard, Dadao happily\naccepted, and they began their new lives.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Jun_001: After succeeding Solel as the new Divine\nSovereign, Jurah met with King Bertrand\nof Brezarant as a representative of the\nDagdan pantheon. She accepted the Dagdan\nAlliance that he proposed, promising the\nbacking of the temples. The Dagdan temples\ngradually diminished in influence afterward\nbut continued to be a place of worship for\nthe people.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Jun_002: As voices calling for peace grew louder,\nJurah announced that she would succeed\nSolel as the new Divine Sovereign to unite\nwhat remained of the Dagdan Empire. But\nwithout the Divine Emperor to rally around,\nthe empire's position as a suzerain state\ngrew shaky. The land of Dagda entered an\nera of warlords feuding over territory, and it\nwould be a long time before the continent\nwas unified under a single banner again.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Mar_001: After the battle with Balor, Mars announced\nhis retirement from politics and distanced\nhimself from the centers of power. In this\nway, he helped bring about the age of rule\nby humanity rather than divinity. He never\nagain took to the battlefield as the Bringer\nof War, but he supported Jurah, the new\nDivine Sovereign, from behind the scenes.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Smi_001: After the war for the fate of the world,\nSmyrnos followed his nature and devoted\nhimself to inquiries into the nature of magic,\ntirelessly researching day and night.\nDecades later, an experimental spell based\non a new theory caused the spectacular\ndeath of Smyrnos in an unanticipated\nfirestorm, taking his whole temple with him.\nThis last spell was dubbed the Forbidden\nSpell of Smyrnos and remains sealed away\nas voided knowledge.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Cla_001: After the war, Credna returned to his\ntemple and resumed his life as before.\nLeaving the daily chores to the priests, he\nspent his time surrounded by things he\nloved, tinkering with machines as he\npleased. Yet those who knew him well\nnoticed that he seemed somewhat lonely.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Cla_002: After the battle, Credna returned to his\ndaily life, growing even more absentminded\nand detached than before, as if he had lost\nhis sense of purpose. Later, he abruptly set\noff on a journey, and Archpriest Gephma\nnever saw him again for the rest of her days.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Car_001: Years after the war, Kalla announced that\nshe would resign from her position as a god,\nshocking all of Dagda. She changed her\nname and wandered the land, retracing\nthe path her son Cohen once walked. In her\nwake, she left numerous legends of a\nmysterious performer whose skill surpassed\neven the Virtuosa of Heaven and Earth.\nHaving regained her confidence during her\nlong wanderings, she returned to her temple\nand found new ways to foster the arts\nin Dagda.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Aur_001: Though Aurora had briefly abandoned her\nposition as a god, she resolved to remain in\nher temple so long as people saw a need for\nher. She provided invaluable support to\nJurah, the newly crowned Divine Sovereign.\nIn her heart, she still saw her father, Solel,\nas a figure to emulate. When not at her\ntemple, Aurora was sometimes seen in\nDagsion, heatedly scolding Credna for his\nabsentmindedness.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Ism_001: During the collapse of the underworld,\n{AvatarName} disappeared along with\nthe goddess Fortuna. Neither of them were\never seen again. But a certain prophet\nclaimed that they had simply returned to\nwhere they came from and would come\nagain as the Herald of the Pale Raven\nwhen the world needed them most. This\nlegend spread across the land of Dagda\nand remained in the hearts of its people\nfor generations to come.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Kai_001: Cai, who disliked the idea of being treated\nas a hero, refused offers from all quarters\nand set out to travel the land of Dagda.\nMuch later, when a single monarch had\nunited all of Dagda, he was welcomed as\na great general. In Imperial Calendar year\n1727, during the Adrestian Empire's\ninvasion from Fódlan, Cai faced a force of\nover 20 thousand. Yielding not a single step,\nhe drove into the enemy, striking fear into\ntheir hearts. But even his strength\neventually faltered and he was struck down.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Kai_002: Unable to accept being treated as a hero, \nCai refused offers from all quarters and set\nout to travel the land of Dagda. Throughout\nhis life, he continued to perform remarkable\ndeeds wherever he went, saving many lives.\nAs a result, Cai's name ironically went down\nin the histories as a great hero.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Bel_001: After the war, Bertrand focused on domestic\naffairs. Once his kingdom was sufficiently\nsettled, he worked on realizing his grand\nidea. A year later, alongside Arago, he\nannounced the Dagdan Alliance. Once he\nhad the backing of Divine Sovereign Jurah,\nwho succeeded Solel as head of the Dagdan\nEmpire, he became the first king of the\nAlliance and devoted himself to quelling the\nchaos in the land. Bertrand patiently worked\nto win over rulers opposed to the Alliance\nplan, ensuring peace without bloodshed.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Bel_002: After the war, Bertrand focused on domestic\naffairs. Once his kingdom was sufficiently\nsettled, he worked on realizing his grand\nidea. This vision was key to a new\nframework of stability for the region.\nThough the road to fruition was long and\narduous, Bertrand always favored diplomacy\nover military options, as vividly described\nin many historical records.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Dit_001: Dietrich grew fond indeed of the land of\nDagda, as he wandered there throughout\nhis days. This proved a problem for some\nof its rulers, who came to dread his\nunpredictable ways. With Dietrich's craving\nfor battle remaining undiminished, scholars\nassumed his final moments came in glorious\ndefeat on a battlefield somewhere. Shortly\nafter his death, the hideously damaged\nAnswerer was borne to Garreg Mach. The\nblade was locked away out of public view,\nand came to be known as a Lost Relic.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Dit_002: Dietrich proved fond indeed of the land of\nDagda, as he wandered there for the rest of\nhis days. This proved to be a problem for\nsome of its rulers, who came to dread his\nunpredictable ways. The black-garbed\nknight shrouded in death became a symbol\nof fear, and people spoke of him through the\nages as an opposing counterpart to the\nwhite-clad savior of the world.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Tal_001: One day, Talimun let out a big yawn, said,\n"I've worked too hard," and fell into a period\nof hibernation. Ten years later, he awoke\nagain and returned to the Vandahl Trading\nCompany. With its resources, he realized\nhis plan for the Bran canal and founded\nthe nation of Talimundia. As planned, the\nVandahl Trading Company got richer,\nbut Talimun himself craved excitement and\nleft his nation's affairs to his employees so\nthat he could return to a life of adventure.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Tal_002: After returning to his normal routine at his\ncompany, Talimun continued life as before:\ndisappearing for years at a time, devoting\nhimself to ambitious business ventures, and\nembarking on carefree escapades. He was\nremembered in the histories of Dagda—\nthough more as a renowned adventurer than\nas a great merchant.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Orh_001: Orchel returned to Credna's main temple\nand resumed her life there. Though she was\nseemingly content, Credna noticed a hint of\nloneliness on her face occasionally. At every\nopportunity, she would visit Dagsion via the\nGate of the Gods, where she was seen lost\nin thought. About two hundred years later,\nOrchel's body shut down and Credna sealed\nit away deep within the temple, where it\nwould never move again. "Rest well,\nOrchel," he said, "until we meet again."
MID_END_Solo_Living_Orh_002: Orchel returned to Credna's main temple\nand resumed her cheerful life there.\nShe continues to appear in temple records\nfor about two hundred years after the war,\nbeyond which point there is no mention of\nher. Some theorize that the mysterious girl\nhad some connection to the Dagdan\npantheon, but the truth remains a mystery.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Seo_001: Theodora annexed the land of Cybele for\nSaramis, and having accomplished her\npeople's long-held dream, began rebuilding\nthe temple of Yu Phas in Ahm Lu as a\nholy site for the children of Damascar.\nUnder her rule, Saramis saw unprecedented\ngrowth. But when Theodora's arm caused\nher health to decline, she ceded the throne\nto a hand-picked heir. She never again\nappeared before her people and is believed\nto have lived a life of seclusion near\nMahadu's shrine.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Seo_002: Theodora returned to the kingdom of\nSaramis and set to work restoring the land\nthat had been devastated by years of war.\nShe was beloved by her people, and under\nher leadership they restored Saramis to its\nprewar state before other nations could\nfully recover. Theodora's name went down\nin history as one of Saramis's greatest\nmonarchs, and the people spoke of her\ndeeds for many generations.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Led_001: Once Leda resolved her vendetta against\nBertrand, she locked Obsidian away in\nKalla's temple and began performing across\nDagda. According to one historian's research\nbased on songs about her, Leda's travels\ncontinued for around 40 years, never\nsettling in one place for long. Though no one\nknows what became of Leda in her later\nyears, the legend of the Siren of the Six-\nString lived on in Dagda for generations.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Led_002: After the war, Leda continued her travels,\nplaying her vihuela wherever she went\nwithout ever settling down. According to\none historian's research based on songs\npassed down by minstrels, her nomadic\nlifestyle continued for another 40 years.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Anh_001: As Forbidden Queen of the ancient kingdom\nof Solomon, Anatolia led her people in the\ncompletion of Tiamat. Despite many\nsetbacks, she saw the project through with\nthe people's support. Two hundred years\nlater, Tiamat was ready for launch, and\nAnatolia ascended into space with her\ncompanions to safeguard humanity's\nachievements. In time, they became known\nas celestials, legendary figures believed to\ndescend again when they are needed.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Anh_002: After ending the war for the future of\nhumanity, Anatolia was said to return to\nthe ancient kingdom of Solomon, of which\nshe was the ruler, before vanishing from\nhistory completely. One theory suggests that\nthe people of Solomon ascended to the\nheavens with their queen and watch over\nthis world still. The legend of these\ncelestials, who would one day descend\nagain when needed most, continued to be\npassed down through the generations.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Tia_001: Tialla achieved her dream of serving the\ntemples, spending her days alternating\nbetween humble service and devouring the\ncontents of their libraries. In the course of\nher contented life, she wrote a great many\nhistories detailing a series of battles. Her\naccounts were precise, down-to-earth, and\nfull of Tialla's vibrant sensibilities. Thus did\nthe prolific writings of Tialla August\nbecome required reading for historians of\nsubsequent ages.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Pet_001: After surviving battles that decided the fate\nof the world, Peter returned to a normal life\nin his hometown of Ribeira. Though he\nnever quite let go of his childhood affection\nfor Tialla, he wedded an ardent suitor who'd\nbeen one of his childhood companions.\nIn short order, they were blessed with\nfive children, and though they quarreled\nfrom time to time, their home was overall\na happy one.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Hur_001: As Aurora's attendant and friend, Ultand\ndevoted her life to the temple and to her\ngoddess. Ultand's loyal and attentive nature\nmade her one of the temple's most reliable\npriests, and she ultimately came to serve as\nhigh priest of Aurora's temple. Even after\nher elevation to the role, she remained\nearnest and kind, lending an ear and a hand\nto whoever needed one.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Max_001: Maxim returned to his homeland of Arago\nto reunite with his family. He used his\nunique skills to open a tailor's shop in the\ncapital of Grand Aragon, where he produced\ninnovative clothing that turned heads of\nall genders. The shop soon became one of\nArago's trendiest establishments.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Gol_001: Goliath returned to his hometown, where he\nwas hailed as a hero of the Underworld\nWar. Having grown as a person through\ncountless battles, Goliath made peace with \nthose who cast him out and was asked by\nhis people to become the leader of the\nChetaur. He led them into a period of \nunprecedented prosperity using all that he'd\nlearned from Bertrand and his friends.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Gat_001: Gaitz was wholeheartedly loyal to Bertrand\nand served him for many years. The king\nrelied on Gaitz not just as a retainer, but\nas a close friend and counselor in difficult\nsituations. Historians believe that Bertrand's\nremarkable achievements were due largely\nto General Gaitz's loyalty and dedication.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Gat_002: Though Gaitz was a descendant of the\nBrezarant royal family, he never sought to\nlead, and instead served the king elected\nafter Bertrand's death. Thirty-one years\nlater, Gaitz requested a leave of absence and\nset off on a journey of knight errantry, just\nas he had done in his youth. No one in\nDagda heard from him again.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Dan_001: After the war, Dante holed up in her estate\nand began writing several works at once,\ndrawing on her experiences of the war.\nShe wrote as if possessed, and each work\nshe penned during this period was a\nmasterpiece passed down for generations.\nAll her life, a constant stream of journeyman\nwriters begged to be her apprentice, but she\nwas so manic in her creativity that only one\ncould ever keep up with her.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Fab_001: After a series of status reports containing a\nwealth of data on the lands of Dagda,\ncommunication from Fabio to Vritra ceased.\nIt seems that he never returned to Agartha.\nWhether this was his own will or the result\nof circumstances beyond his control is\nunknown. Whether or not he ever returned\nto Fódlan, it is known that Fabio's formal\nname was erased from Agarthan records.\nNo search for him was undertaken.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Esm_001: Esmeralda returned to her mother in her\nhometown and began her life as a master\nfisher. With spear in hand, she took down\nany and all sea beasts threatening her home,\ngoing down in history as a legendary angler.\nAt some point, she married a friend from\nher childhood, and the two were blessed\nwith five children. Esmeralda would regale\nthem with tales of her vivacious life and\nher proud ancestor, painting them a picture\nof the land of Fódlan beyond the sea.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Urs_001: Ursula continued to prosper as manager of\nthe Vandahl Trading Company. Though\nmany attempted to court her, she chose to\nremain steadfast in her work, rather than\npursue any semblance of romance. After 50\nmore years of service, Ursula retired to a\nremote location where she lived out the rest\nof her days in peace. It is said, however,\nthat she would often cross the sea in secret\nto visit her motherland of Fódlan, although\nthis theory has yet to be proven and remains\nmerely rumor.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Sim_001: Even after the battle with Balor, Simon\nworked as a mercenary, choosing only the\nmost violent of conflicts. It was whispered\nthat "wherever war rages, there you'll find\nthe Sky-Drum." But no battlefield could truly\nfulfill him, and he never found satisfaction\nin combat. One day while traveling to the\nnext war, Simon was bitten by a snake and\ndied on the road. His final words were a\ngrim joke at his own expense: "Who knew\nI'd die anywhere but in battle?"
MID_END_Solo_Living_Lou_001: Ludia continued her work at Vandahl\nTrading, working diligently each day. Her\nextraordinary talent and keen eye earned\nher high praise within the company, and she\nwas soon promoted to manager of their\nnewly established Saramis branch. Through\nit all, Ludia's relationship with her father\nremained as strong as ever.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Fia_001: After parting with her companions, Fianna\nbegan to serve the temples in Dagsion, using\nher powers to help the people and heal the\ninjured. Always kind and sincere, Fianna\ncame to be likened to a saint, and there are\nmany stories of people coming to her to\nhave their troubles heard. The line of those\nin need never seemed to end.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Fia_002: Having regained her memories of her time\nas Fatima, Fianna returned to Arago and\nspent the rest of her life working toward the\nrestoration of her homeland. She toiled with\nsingle-minded purpose, as if trying to atone\nfor her brother's sins, and the people were\ntouched by her dedication. Eleven years\nlater, a civil war broke out. In the chaos,\nFianna was felled by someone holding a\ngrudge against her brother, Gilchris, despite\nher own resentment toward him. Yet she\nmet her end stoically, as if long ready for it.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Die_001: While serving as a priest at Credna's temple,\nDiego worked to dispel prejudice against the\ngoddess Yu Phas and the children of\nDamascar. Though he remained aloof to the\nend, many who were struck by his sincerity\nfound themselves drawn to his cause.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Lor_001: After returning to Credna's temple, Loretta\nworked diligently at her duties and grew\ninto a priest trusted by her associates and\nmany of the temple's visitors. Her blithe\nattitude slowly faded as she grew into the\nrole. Upon Ozin making good on his promise\nto adopt her, she lived out a contented life\nthanks to his care.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Set_001: After the war, Seteth saw order gradually\nreturn to Dagda. Though his companions\nwere sad to see him leave, he returned to\nFódlan and reunited with his daughter, who\nhad awakened from her long slumber at\nGarreg Mach Monastery. Later, Seteth\ncompiled his experiences in Dagda and\npresented them to the archbishop. The\nbook was never made public, and is said\nto be secretly stored in the archbishop's\nprivate library at the monastery.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Nin_001: After the battle with Balor, Ninae returned\nto Credna's temple. Many powerful leaders\nsought to recruit the famed Black-Lace\nNinae, but she refused all offers and stayed\nloyal as a vulkan protecting the temples.\nMany men had more than casual feelings for\nthe beautiful knight and looked for ways to\nearn her favor, but she remained oblivious\nand carried on as usual.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Bon_001: Bonaventure put his exceptional intellect to\nthe task of supporting Theodora alongside\nChancellor Kumos for many years. Roughly\none hundred years after his death, the\nthorough history of Saramis that he penned\nin secret was discovered. His records were\nmeticulous, as if he had transcribed the\nstorehouse of his mind, and future historians\ncame to consider it required reading.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Bon_002: With the loss of Theodora as a unifying\nforce, Saramis found itself without a central\npillar. Bonaventure worked hard to find a\nsuccessor who could rebuild, eventually\ndiscovering a young man who bore the \nblood of a lost branch of the royal line.\nMoved by the aged Bonaventure's zeal, he\nperformed the Monarch's Axe ceremony\nflawlessly and succeeded Theodora. Though\nBonaventure was proud of what he had\naccomplished, it is said he still wept to think\nof what his kingdom had lost.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Tob_001: After the war, Tobias continued to support\nthe throne of Saramis as a commander. He\nwas no more of a strategist than ever, so\nwhen he realized 10 years later that his\nphysical condition was deteriorating, he\nchose to retire. Tobias never married, nor\ndid he decrease his drinking habits—some\nsay he died peacefully, face down on the\nground with a cask of ale in hand. Though it\nwas a lonely and ignominious end, those\nwho knew him well admitted it was within\nhis character, even as they mourned him.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Lil_001: Lilian used the money she earned through\nher battles to buy back her childhood estate\nand reestablish a peaceful life with her\nfamily. She retired from the military but\ncontinued to hunt as a hobby. Lilian wed\na man who served with her as a soldier, and\nthey lived in harmony together. Those who\nknew Lilian often relied on her for her\nunimpeachable character and caring nature.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Lys_001: Lysander used his innate daring and good\nsense to distinguish himself as a warrior.\nEventually, he was appointed chancellor\nand played a part in steering the kingdom.\nMany asked if his quick rise was due to his\nmentorship from Bonaventure and Tobias,\nknown as great commanders, to which\nLysander would always smile and nod with\na nostalgic look in his eyes.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Buc_001: After the Underworld War, Buccar chose to\ncontinue as Leda's retainer. She urged\nBuccar to start a family, saying she didn't\nwant to be used as an excuse for him to stay\nsingle, and even went so far as to introduce\nhim to a few prospective partners. In the\nend, though, he remained a bachelor for the\nrest of his life. After his death, Leda had\nhim buried beside Guillermo.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Buc_002: After the Underworld War, Buccar settled in\nDagsion and put his skills to work upholding\nthe peace. He was taciturn but reliable, and\nmany younger soldiers came to idolize him.\nLater on, he happened to meet a widow\nwho ran a tavern in Dagsion. A few years\nlater, they began living together and were\neventually blessed with three children.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Sci_001: After the battle with Balor, Sirocco returned\nto his work as a vulkan of Kalla's temple.\nHis life became even busier than before.\nSeveral years later, when Kalla elected to\nleave the temples, Sirocco joined her, and\nthe two wandered the land of Dagda\ntogether. Though Kalla seemed outwardly\nannoyed by Sirocco, a journal discovered\na hundred years after his death revealed\nthat she was always pleased to have\nhim around.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Moo_001: As her mother, Mikaela, once hoped, Mu\napprenticed at Smyrnos's temple and spent\nher days poring over the vast collection of\nbooks kept there. The god himself was said\nto have taken a shine to her for her\ndiligence. While working at the temple, she\ninvented a number of medicines, eventually\nsaving more lives than magic could ever\nhope to. History would remember her as an\nimportant figure in the advancement of\npharmaceuticals in Dagda.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Mic_001: Mikaela went on to travel Dagda as a\nmercenary, spending her days fighting.\nMany influential figures across the land\noffered her favorable positions, but she\ndeclined them all. Using the money earned\nfrom her mercenary work, she established a\nfoundation to support those who had lost\ntheir place in the world, acting as its\ndirector in between mercenary jobs. She\nmet her end on the battlefield defending her\nallies' retreat, laying down her life to stop\nthe enemy's pursuit.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Oly_001: For her tireless efforts, Olympia was made a\nlead priest in Kalla's temple, where she\ncontinued to act as a patron of the arts.\nShe eventually rose to the rank of high\npriest, a position that earned her the respect\nof all who knew her in Caelus. Believing\nthat the goddess Kalla, who left the temples\nof her own volition, would return, Olympia\nvowed to safeguard the temple until that\nday arrived. Alas, she did not live to see her\ngoddess's return.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Naz_001: To make the most of his few years left,\nNezha crossed the sea and traveled beyond\nthe land of Dagda in search of a stronger\nopponents. Though his lack of a Heart Core\ntook a heavy toll on him during the harsh\njourney, he never stopped moving forward.\nWhen Nezha arrived in the eastern land of\nRama, he met a new master and found\nenlightenment, spending the rest of his days\nin peace.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Sar_001: After relocating to Dagsion, Sha Lan finally\nopened the restaurant she'd long dreamed\nof. Her food became wildly popular,\nattracting long lines of customers each day...\nthough many of them came just for the\nsparkling conversation. Thanks to her sharp\nbusiness sense, Sha Lan began a franchise\nand eventually founded a major trading\nhouse. Many of her employees had ties to\nthe People of the White Egg, and she led\na busy and prosperous life.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Dai_001: Dadao became an apprentice to Credna,\nthe god of blacksmithing, and learned a lot\nunder his tutelage. His sharp mind,\ncombined with the knowledge of the People\nof the White Egg and the skills Credna\ntaught him, later helped him make a\ndifference in people's lives. He trained many\napprentices and was widely respected.\nThough he never married, he always hoped\nit would be in the cards and never quite\nmade his peace with the bachelor life.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Hal_001: Using the funds earned from her stint as a\nhero of the Underworld War, Halvin bought\nthe land her family had rented, fulfilling her\nlong-held dream of returning home. The\noliva plants her family grew became known\nthroughout Dagda for their large, high-\nquality fruit, and soon came to be\ndistributed under the name "Halvin-Brand."
MID_END_Solo_Living_Guj_001: After the long war, Guzran returned to his\nnormal life. Even after earning fame as one\nof the heroes of the Underworld War, his\nbehavior never changed. He held allegiance\nto no country, wandered constantly through\nentertainment districts, never flattered or\npandered, lied when he felt like it, and\nsteadily completed what mercenary requests\ncame his way. He lived for about 20 years\nafter the war, and despite his abrasive ways,\nGuzran's innate cheerfulness and kindness\nmade him beloved by many.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Yan_001: One day, Yang Jie vanished without a word,\nand no one in Dagda ever saw him again.\nThere were many theories about his final\nmoments. Some say he drank too much and\ncollapsed somewhere, others believed he\ncrossed the sea to Fódlan, and a few\nsuggested he had powerful patrons in the\nland of Sai, who appointed him as their\ncourt magician. But none of these theories\nhad any supporting evidence, and his story\nremains a mystery to this day.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Iio_001: Io returned to his homeland of Arago. When\nhe saw its people suffering in the chaos that\nfollowed the war, he decided to serve his\ncountry as a knight once more. Through his\nmany battles, Io finally found his oath as a\nknight—to serve the people rather than any\nmaster. He achieved many remarkable feats,\nand his name was known not only within\nArago, but throughout the land of Dagda.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Pep_001: Peppe's experiences in the land of Dagda\nhelped him mature as a king. After his\nreturn to Brigid, he demonstrated what he\nlearned not just in relations with other\ncountries, but in domestic policy as well,\nleading his kingdom to further prosperity.\nDespite all that kept him busy, from time to\ntime he was said to sigh deeply as he\nrecalled a woman he had met in Dagda,\njust before waxing poetic to those around\nhim of her many charms.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Noc_001: Noctula bought a house in Dagsion and\nenjoyed city life for a time while helping\nwith the rebuilding efforts. But at a certain\npoint, she tired of maintaining relationships\nand returned to the village where she was\nraised. Her experience in the Underworld\nWar earned her special treatment within her\nclan, and on her siblings' recommendation,\nshe became the new chief of the Asherah.\nHer no-nonsense personality kept the\nclan united in their love for their chief.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Sop_001: Sofia traveled around the land of Dagda,\npreaching the virtues of Solel, whom she\nadmired and respected. Her work bore fruit\nafter 20 years when the temples recognized\nher followers as the Solel sect. In later years,\nSofia's name came to be known by\nhistorians as a notable priest who\ndevoted her whole life to spreading her\nbeliefs, but these same histories noted that\nshe was often seen collapsed on the road in\nher travels due to hunger.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Cat_001: Having survived a grueling battle for the\nfate of the world, Catania traveled Dagda in\nsearch of a lord to serve. A chance meeting\nled her to an influential soldier in the\nCastalia region. She served her lord well,\ngoing on to accomplish many spectacular\nfeats of combat, and her name went down\nin the histories of Dagda.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Ned_001: Nydine returned to Saramis after her long\nabsence and was promoted as an officer to\nonce again serve her homeland. Later, after\nretiring from active service, she taught\nfuture generations in combat, raising many\ntalented warriors. Though several men\nsought her hand in marriage, none ever met\nher standards, and she remained unmarried\nthroughout her life.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Zac_001: Zarcone returned to his base in Caelus and\nwent back to his life of crime. Hearing word\nof his exploits, other ruffians in the region\njoined up with him, and the Gaia Brigade\nbecame a major force. They were successful\nenough that the central government took\nnotice and sent a strike team to deal with\nthem. Zarcone refused all calls for surrender\nand fought to the last, but was killed and left\nto rot where he fell. Though he was cruel\nand merciless to his victims, his crew\nalways spoke kindly of him.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Maj_001: After the battle with Balor, Majide was\nhailed as a hero by those around him. He\nlived comfortably in Dagsion for a time and\nwas well liked until his violent nature got\nthe better of him. Just as before, he was in\nand out of prison and eventually banished\nfrom Dagsion. He was believed to have\nleft for southern regions, complaining all\nthe while.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Ven_001: Due to his distinguished service in seeing\nthe fight against Balor through to the end,\nBenditz achieved his heart's desire and was\nappointed a general of the Dagdan Empire.\nUnfortunately, it was at that time that he\nbegan to suffer severe lower back pain,\nforcing him into an early retirement. Despite\nbeing dumped back into civilian life, he\nboasted more loudly than ever about his\ndays as a distinguished Dagdan general.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Ini_001: After the Underworld War, Inyoni went\nback to her hometown and spent her life as\na hunter. Though she tended to downplay it,\nher bravery in standing up to Balor to save\nthe world was boasted of for generations\nas a point of pride for the local warriors. She\nwas greatly respected by all sorts—men and\nwomen, young and old.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Jas_001: Having made a name for herself as a hero\nwho fought alongside the Promised One,\nJasmine finally achieved her dream of \nreuniting her mercenary group. They\ntraveled the land, protecting those who\nneeded it during this time of chaos. Ten\nyears later, no longer in her prime, Jasmine\ndisbanded the group and retired. Over her\nfriends' protests, she returned to her\nhomeland of Brigid. Several of her friends\nwere so distraught by her departure that\nthey followed her across the sea.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Ale_001: Alexandra returned to Tellus, where her\nmemories of her family were strongest, and\nchose the path of serving the people at her\nlocal temple. It was a difficult life, but she\nfound the work fulfilling. Many suitors\napproached Alexandra, but she accepted\nnone of them and remained single all her\nlife. Though Alexandra was generally mild\nmannered, when her uncle approached her\nto mend their relationship, she rejected the\noverture with bloodcurdling venom.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Cle_001: 
MID_END_Solo_Living_Mys_001: 
MID_END_Solo_Living_Kou_001: Even after fighting with all her strength to\natone for her sins, Hong Hua still felt a\nsense of guilt. She built a hermitage deep in\nthe mountains and lived quietly for a time,\navoiding contact with people. There, she\ncontinued to meditate on what she should\nbe doing. One day, she concluded that the\nproper path was to help those who were as\nlost as she was. She set out on a pilgrimage,\nall the while envisioning the savior in white\nwhom she herself once followed.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Cen_001: Ordered by Aurora to take a wife and start\na family, Centurio was introduced to a\npriest to whom he'd always been favorably\ndisposed and began a new life with her.\nThough he was an awkward husband, they\nnevertheless made a happy home between\nthem. The wedded couple was blessed with\none child, who ran them ragged, but the\nexperience did much to soften Centurio's\ninnate stubbornness.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Asw_001: As queen of Arago, Aswan agreed to\nBertrand's vision for the Dagdan Alliance\nand joined it at an early stage. She\ncontinued to oversee the territory of Arago\neven after entering into the alliance. Aswan\nwas a wise governor, especially when it\ncame to domestic policy. Through her\nguidance, the former kingdom of Arago\nentered into a period of renewed stability\nand prosperity.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Asw_002: As queen of Arago, Aswan devoted herself\nto stabilizing her country. But 20 years later,\nduring a tour of the kingdom's border, she\nwas attacked by a man with a deep-seated\ngrudge against the royal family and fell to\nhis blade. Many citizens and soldiers of\nArago mourned the death of their wise and\nkindhearted queen.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Tah_001: Tahonia spent her life by Aswan's side,\ncaring for her and keeping her safe. She\nvigorously shut down threats on Aswan's\nlife, becoming known as Tahonia the\nImpassable. She taught her Python style\nof fighting to a talented youth she met in\nGrand Aragon's castle town, ensuring it\nwould be passed down in the future. The\nyouth would later come to be a well-known\nmartial artist, but that is a story for\nanother time.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Nat_001: After returning to his homeland, Nathan \nonce again pledged his loyalty to the throne\nand worked to bring order to the parts of\nArago still in turmoil. All the while, he\ndevoted himself to training the next\ngeneration of warriors. From his vantage\npoint on the front lines of battle, he saw\nmany major events firsthand, inspiring a\ngood number of bards to portray him. Yet\ndespite it all, his earnest forthrightness\nnever faltered.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Hri_001: Even after experiencing so much strife,\nCreek never gave up his cynical nature,\nthough some noted that he softened ever\nso slightly. Creek himself explained this\naway by saying it was the consequence of\nbeing forced to follow stupid orders. A few\nyears later, Creek fell ill during a border\ninspection and passed away before he could\nbe returned to Grand Aragon. Because he\nkept up his gallows humor until the end,\nthose around him never realized the gravity\nof his illness.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Gra_001: 
MID_END_Solo_Living_Kir_001: After returning to the Danann Sea, Kiroc\nrecruited some roughnecks, reformed his\nband of ne'er-do-wells, and picked up the\npirate life where he left off. He frequently\nclashed with Vandahl Trading on the high\nseas, though his deep-rooted fear of ghosts\nprevented him from fighting on the front\nlines. In the end, the Dagdan Empire's navy\nstruck at his base, and despite his heroic\nefforts, he and his crew fell in battle.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Nuz_001: Nuzzuo volunteered to guard Balor's temple\nand lived alone on the Isle of Balor. He kept\nwatch over the empty temple until the end\nof his days, mourning the demon god his\npeople worshipped before their great\napostasy. However, it should be noted that\nafter some time, a few like-minded Har Hali\ncrossed the sea to reach Nuzzuo, where they\nbuilt a settlement on the island and lived a\nstoic life together.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Kra_001: When Klapka returned to the Mosa, having\nseen the war for the fate of the world as a\nguest general, he reported the whole story\nto King Oktar. The king was greatly\nimpressed by Klapka winning renown for\nthe Mosa in a foreign land, and rewarded\nthe brave general handsomely. Klapka\ncontinued to fight on the front lines as a\nMosa officer and is believed to have\nperished in a battle against the kingdom of\nLezeraon to the south.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Tro_001: Having secured a future for humanity, Troy\nquietly slipped away from her allies. Many\nbelieved that she returned to her peaceful\nlife at her shrine—though she kept up her\nduty as guardian of Kunlun for years to\ncome, watching over her kin and the Grand\nMegaliths across the land. There is no\nrecord of how long her vigil lasted.
MID_END_Solo_Living_Ann_001: 
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Tia_001: Tialla returned to Ribeira, where she read\navidly as she convalesced. But when an\nearthquake struck, she was killed beneath\nthe weight of her shelves.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Pet_001: Peter returned to his tranquil life in Ribeira.\nBut it wasn't long before he fell gravely ill\nand, under his family's care, drew his\nlast breath.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Hur_001: Ultand quietly withdrew to her hometown to\nbe with her family. But a persistent wound\nsustained in the Heroic Games festered,\ncausing her to breathe her last.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Max_001: He returned home and tried to flee Arago\nwith his family. But the Order of the Haze\nhad been keeping an eye on their house\nand wasted no time getting retribution.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Gol_001: He returned to his life as a gladiator in\nDagsion. On the orders of the resurrected\nEmperor Dagda, he and the other gladiators\nwere put to death in Dagda's cauldron.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Gat_001: He returned to his motherland after the\nHeroic Games. While he was inspecting\none of the settlements in his territory, a\nmonster attacked, and he sacrificed himself\nto let his underlings escape.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Dan_001: She remained in Dagsion, where she busied\nherself with penning a new script. On the\norders of the resurrected Emperor Dagda,\nshe was put to death in Dagda's cauldron.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Fab_001: Fabio quietly slipped away from his allies.\nNot a trace of him was ever seen thereafter\nin the land of Dagda.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Esm_001: Though she returned to her fishing village\nto recuperate from the wounds she received\nin the Heroic Games, an ill-fated fishing\nexpedition spelled disaster for Esmeralda.\nHer boat was struck by a tidal wave and\ncapsized, which was the last anyone ever\nsaw of her.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Urs_001: While she was sailing aboard a Vandahl\nTrading Company merchant vessel, the ship\nwas boarded by pirates. Though she fought\nfiercely to fend them off, she was\noverwhelmed and tragically killed.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Sim_001: He left Vandahl Trading to return to a freer\nlife as a mercenary. Unfortunately, a\nmember of his company betrayed him on\nthe battlefield, and he perished.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Lou_001: She returned to her family's home but was\ngravely injured during training and fell into\na coma. She never regained consciousness\nand passed away several years later.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Fia_001: While on a job for the Vandahl Trading\nCompany, she came under attack from\nassassins dispatched by an unknown party.\nShe lost her life to their blades.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Die_001: Diego visited the southern forest in search\nof a secret remedy to heal his injuries from\nbattle, but a survivor of the Har Hali\nrecognized him from their shared past and\nslew him for betraying them.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Lor_001: Though she managed to escape Dagsion\nand return to Ozin at Credna's temple,\nher wounds were too severe and she\npassed away.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Set_001: The wounds he sustained in Dagda were\nsevere enough for him to seek a merchant\nship back to Fódlan. Luckily, he found a\nsuitable vessel and managed to return home.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Nin_001: She ignored a summons from the\nresurrected Dagda the Great. In response,\nhe branded her a deserter and sent the\nvulkans after her. She met a tragic end\nafter a fierce last stand.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Lil_001: Lilian left the army to live alone but died\nafter a venomous snake bit her while she\nwas hunting in a dense forest.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Lys_001: Lysander returned to his uncle's house in\nSaramis to recuperate, but while out on a\nlong ride, he fell off his horse and died.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Buc_001: After parting ways with Leda, he began to\nwander despite his injuries. He died after\ngetting caught up in a riot that broke out\nin a town where he was staying.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Sci_001: Sirocco was sharing a bed with a woman\nhe'd seduced, as was his custom, when due\nto a stopped-up nose he was unable to\ndetect the poison she'd laced their drinks\nwith. As a result, he perished as part of her\nmurder-suicide plot.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Moo_001: The wounds she received in battle worsened\nuntil she developed a high fever and\ncollapsed. She never regained consciousness\nand eventually breathed her last.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Mic_001: After the end of the Heroic Games, Mikaela\nleft Dagsion and continued to roam the land\nas a mercenary. She fell in battle during a\nlittle-known skirmish.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Oly_001: Forced to put her complicated feelings for\nLeda aside, Olympia decided to return to\nKalla's temple in order to recover from her\ninjuries. However, she met with an accident\nalong the way and was never seen again.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Naz_001: Seeking greater strength, he left his\ncompanions behind and set off on a solitary\njourney of training. However, he fell ill in\na foreign land and never recovered.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Sar_001: Even after the Heroic Games, she worked\non Kunlun's behalf to relay information to\nTroy. However, on the orders of the\nresurrected Emperor Dagda, she was put\nto death in Dagda's cauldron.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Dai_001: He tried to capture a kusarik for its meat,\nbut it was stronger than he anticipated.\nIt dragged him off a cliff, and he was\nnever seen again.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Hal_001: She eked out a living as a street performer\nin Dagsion, but on the orders of the\nresurrected Emperor Dagda, she and the\nrest of the city's populace were put to death\nin Dagda's cauldron.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Guj_001: His heavy daily drinking took its toll on his\nbody. Though he was advised to cut back,\nhe refused. In the end, he vomited blood\nand took his last breath after collapsing at\nthe dinner table.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Yan_001: After getting drunk and killing someone in\nan argument, Yang Jie became a fugitive.\nHe tried to lie low, but the soldiers in\npursuit eventually surrounded him, and he\ndied a brutal death.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Iio_001: After seeing the Heroic Games through to\nthe end, Io set out in search of a place for\nhimself. But he and his beloved horse both\nlost their lives when a treacherous mountain\nroad collapsed.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Pep_001: Though reluctant to leave, Peppe returned\nto his homeland. But the wounds he\nreceived in his battles in Dagda led him to\nabdicate the throne a few years later.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Noc_001: Noctula returned to her life as a gladiator\nin Dagsion. On the orders of the resurrected\nEmperor Dagda, she and the other gladiators\nwere put to death in Dagda's cauldron.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Sop_001: On her way home, she was unable to bear\nthe hunger and died after eating some food\nshe scavenged.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Cat_001: During a dinner party at the home of a\nwealthy man, Catania was in such good\nspirits that she took too large a bite of\ncheese, choked, and then died.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Ned_001: Nydine left Dagsion and continued to roam\nin search of combat. She met her end on\nan unknown battlefield.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Zac_001: Zarcone returned to his home base in\nCaelus, where he resumed his life as a\nbandit. He met his end while sacking a\nvillage, when a warrior passing through\nproved his match.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Maj_001: Majide was set to be executed in Dagda's\ncauldron along with the rest of Dagsion on\norders of the resurrected Emperor Dagda.\nHis spinning sword technique took four\nsoldiers with him, but he was killed\nnevertheless and thrown into the cauldron.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Ven_001: He joined the imperial army in an effort to\ngarner distinguished military service. But on\nthe way to the battlefield, his chariot veered\noff a cliff and he died.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Ini_001: Once the Heroic Games ended, Inyoni went\nback home. She rested for a while before\nmaking her comeback as a mercenary, but\nsoon after returning to the battlefield, she\nwas struck down in combat.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Jas_001: After the Heroic Games, Jasmine worked\nas a mercenary within Arago, but she was\nbetrayed by a client and killed in battle\nalongside her comrades.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Ale_001: While recovering from wounds sustained at\nthe Heroic Games, her symptoms took a\nturn for the worse. She passed away, with\nthose around her lamenting her loss.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Kir_001: He left Dagsion and set up a hideout in the\nruins of a fort overlooking the Danann Sea,\nhoping to make his comeback. A ghost\nhaunting the abandoned fort frightened him\nso badly that he fell from a cliff and died.
MID_END_Solo_1Lost_Nuz_001: Nuzzuo died of the tetanus festering in the\nwounds he sustained in battle. No one can\nsay if his soul reached his deity, the\ndemon god Balor.
MID_END_Solo_2Lost_Bon_001: While he waited in the rear lines to be\ntreated for serious injuries, his condition\ntook a turn for the worse and he died.
MID_END_Solo_2Lost_Tob_001: While he waited in the rear lines to be\ntreated for serious injuries, his condition\ntook a turn for the worse and he died.
MID_END_Solo_2Dead_Set_001: Though gravely wounded in battle, Seteth\nbarely survived. He left the army and\nboarded a merchant ship bound for Fódlan,\nwhere he safely returned to Garreg Mach.
MID_END_Solo_3Dead_Set_001: Though gravely wounded in battle, Seteth\nbarely survived. He left the army and\nboarded a merchant ship bound for Fódlan,\nwhere he safely returned to Garreg Mach.
MID_END_Solo_3Dead_Cle_001: 
MID_END_Solo_3Dead_Mys_001: 
MID_END_Solo_3Dead_Ann_001: 